            "reasoning_content": "Turn 2. I have 946 gold, 35 wood, 20 food, 10 ore, 5 equip, 10 supply.\n\nBuildings from turn 1 now active (they were under construction, now effective). Wait, the panel shows 位1/20 with buildings already listed: 林场×1, 农场×1, 矿场×1. So they're now built.\n\nProduction last turn: \"产出 无\" — hmm, that's the record of turn 1 settlement which had nothing active. Now turn 2 settlement will produce.\n\nPlan for turn 2: build 1 per tile, 5 tiles.\n- 朔原(19,8): 农场 #2 (耕5)\n- 达川(20,8): 农场 #2 (耕2)\n- 霜塘(18,8): 林场 #2 (木3)\n- 霜滩(19,7): 林场 #2 (木2)\n- 沃坝(19,9): 矿场 #2 (矿2)\n\nCost: 60+60+57+57+120 = 354 gold, 25 wood. Leaves ~592 gold, 10 wood.\n\nHmm, wood is tight. Turn 3 needs 木材能源厂 (120+15木) at 朔原. I'd have 10 wood + production. Wood production: 2 林场 = 2/turn. So turn 3 start: 10 + 2 = 12 wood. Not enough for 15. Need to buy wood.\n\nMarket wood price 2.5, buying pushes up. Buy 20 wood ≈ 50-60 gold. That's fine, cheap.\n\nActually let me reconsider: should I buy wood now to be safe? Let me buy wood in turn 2 or 3. Prices regress each turn. Buying 20 wood at 2.5 → pushes price. Cost roughly 20*2.5*1.05 ≈ 52 gold. Fine.\n\nAlternatively, reduce 林场 count and buy wood instead. Let's think about the wood economy:\n- Buildings needed over turns 2-6: 兵营×2 (20木 each = 40木), 木材能源厂 (15木), plus more 农场/林场.\n- Total wood demand is high. 林场 gives 1 wood/turn, costs 50金+5木 → 30回合回本 in gold terms but wood is a physical constraint, not just gold.\n\nActually, is wood a real constraint? Market price 2金/木 baseline. A 林场 costs 55金(折) and gives 1木/turn = 2金/turn value. Buying wood at 2.5 = same. But buying in bulk pushes price up. With 3 countries, market depth is small, so big buys spike price.\n\nI think a mix is right. Let me keep building 林场 on forest tiles (霜塘 has 木3, 霜滩 木2) — up to resource cap.\n\nTurn 2 build plan as above. Then buy ~20 wood to secure energy plant construction.\n\nAlso consider: 装备 price 8.8 (high). I need 5 装备 per army. I have 5 装备 already. Food 20. So once barracks is up I can recruit 1 army immediately from stock.\n\nLet me also think about whether to build the second 兵营 at 达川. 达川 needs 3 buildings first: 农场×2 + 林场(木1) = 3位 by turn 4, then 兵营 turn 5, active turn 6. Meanwhile 朔原: 农场×2 + 能源厂 turn 3 = 3位, 兵营 turn 4, active turn 5.\n\nHmm, actually maybe better: put the 木材能源厂 at 达川 instead? Doesn't matter, grid is national.\n\nLet's think about total power need: 兵营×2 = 2电. One 木材能源厂 = 2电. Good. Later if I add 市政厅 (1电 each) I need more.\n\nActually wait — should I prioritize 市政厅 over 兵营? 市政厅 needs 6位 on a tile. 朔原 耕5 → 农场×5 + 市政厅. That's 6 buildings. 市政厅 = 5金 + 6建筑×1 = 11金/回合, costs 500+40木, needs 1电. 回本 ~50回合. Not great early. Skip for now.\n\nPriority: military expansion early. Each new tile = more building slots + resources.\n\nLet me reconsider the timing. Barracks active turn 5, recruit turn 5 → army exists turn 5. Then attack turn 5-6. Each army costs 60 gold equivalent. 2 barracks = 2 armies/turn from turn 5-6.\n\nAlternative faster path: Is there any way to get territory without armies? No.\n\nHmm, but consider: 楚 and 齐 also building. Everyone has same 4-turn minimum to barracks. So it's symmetric. Fine.\n\nShould I build a 3rd barracks? Each barracks 350金+20木 on plains. With 5 tiles now and more later, maybe 2 is right for now, expand later.\n\nLet me also consider: instead of 2 farms at 达川 then 林场, maybe 农场 at 达川 twice is fine (耕2).\n\n达川: 耕2, 木1. So 农场×2 max, then 林场×1. Turn 1 农场, turn 2 农场, turn 3 林场 → 3位, turn 4 兵营, active turn 5.\n\n朔原: 耕5, 木1. Turn 1 农场, turn 2 农场, turn 3 木材能源厂, turn 4 兵营 → active turn 5.\n\nBoth barracks active turn 5.\n\n霜塘(木3): turn1 林场, turn2 林场, turn3 林场 = 3位 → turn4 兵营? That's a 3rd barracks. Cost 350+20木. Maybe later.\n\nLet's keep it lean: 2 barracks.\n\nTurn 2 actions:\n1. Build 5 buildings (农场×2 朔原/达川, 林场×2 霜塘/霜滩, 矿场×2 沃坝)\n2. Buy wood ~20 to prepare for 能源厂 (15木) and later barracks (20木 each)\n\nActually wood budget: turn 2 spend 25木 → 10 left. Turn 3: +2 production = 12木, spend on 能源厂15 → need 3 more. Turn 4: 兵营 20木. Turn 5: 兵营 20木.\n\nTotal wood needed turns 3-5: 15+20+20 = 55, plus other builds. Production ~2-3/turn. So need to buy ~40-50 wood over turns 3-5. Let me buy 25 now and more later. Buying 25 wood at 2.5 → price impact. Let's do it.\n\nActually, let me reconsider — should I build more 林场 instead of buying? 林场 at 霜塘 costs 57金+5木 gives 1木/turn. Over 10 turns = 10木 = 25金 value. Cost 57金. Not worth vs buying at 2.5. But market capacity/price spike matters. Baseline 2金/木.\n\nHmm, but there's a cap issue: 霜塘 木3 → 3 林场上限.\n\nI'll build 林场 up to cap on 霜塘/霜滩 (they're needed as building slots anyway? no). Actually let me not overbuild 林场 — instead buy wood. But 沃坝 has 木2 too (山地, cost ×1.5 = 75金+5木 for 林场... worse).\n\nDecision: Turn 2 build: 朔原农场, 达川农场, 霜塘林场, 霜滩林场, 沃坝矿场. Buy 25 wood.\n\nLet me compute buy cost. Market wood 2.5, depth scaled by 3 countries. Buying 25 → price rises. Total maybe 25*2.8 ≈ 70金. Acceptable.\n\nActually, maybe buy in two chunks of 15 each to reduce impact? Buying pushes price up for the whole transaction (\"整笔按推高后清仓价结算\"). So smaller chunks are cheaper per unit. But two chunks of 15 vs one of 25 — first chunk cheaper. Let me just do 20 at once, then check.\n\nLet me do: buy 木头 20.\n\nAlso should I sell ore? 沃坝矿场×2 gives 2矿/turn, ore price 4. Selling 10 ore = 40金. I have 10 ore stock. Ore is only used for 装备厂/补给厂 which I'm not building. So sell surplus ore gradually. Let me sell 8 ore now at 4.0 → ~32金 minus price impact. Actually keep some? No use for ore. Sell it.\n\nHmm, but selling pushes price down for future sales. Small amounts. Let me sell 8 ore.\n\nActually wait: 装备 — I need 5 per army. Market price 8.8. Should I build 装备厂 instead? 装备厂: 矿1+油1→装备2, needs 1电, 240金+12木. Oil must be bought at 6. Ore at 4. Cost per 装备 = (4+6)/2 = 5金 + electricity. Market price 8.8. So 装备厂 saves ~3.8金/装备. At 2装备/turn = 7.6金/turn gross. 回本 ~35回合. Marginal.\n\nBut oil at 6金 is baseline; my purchase pushes it