o I have some buffer.\n\nThe real tension is whether to prioritize military expansion or economic growth. I'm calculating that 楚 and 齐 will have barracks by turn 6-7, which means my window to grab territory with 3 armies is closing fast. With 3 armies I can sustain 1 tile per turn with better endurance, so I should push military hard now rather than pivot to 黄金矿场.\n\nBut the economics are brutal: each new army costs 44金 for equipment plus food, and upkeep is 15金 per turn. My territory income is only 24金 per turn, so I'm running a deficit that'll drain my treasury in 6-8 turns. The key is that new tiles should provide resources and gold mines to offset this, but I need to scout the newly captured tile at (19,6) first to see what it actually yields.\n\nFor now, my immediate moves are recruiting the army at 朔原, selling excess wood and ore, and buying 5 supplies to stabilize cash flow.",
