            "reasoning_content": "Food crashed to 1.0. Ouch — food is structurally oversupplied (楚 and 齐 also have farms and sell). So selling food is a losing game. I should STOP selling food and instead consume it... but armies consume 补给, not food.\n\nHmm! Actually — wait. 补给厂 converts 粮+矿 → 补给. Food at 1.0 is dirt cheap. 补给 at 5.8. 补给厂: 1粮(1.0) + 1矿(2.8) → 2补给(11.6). That's a 7.8x value multiplier on inputs! \n\nEven better: I could BUY food at 1.0 and 矿... hmm, 矿 at 2.8. 补给厂 inputs = 3.8 for 11.6 of output. And I consume the 补给 (avoiding 16.5金/turn of purchases).\n\nSo 补给厂 is now MUCH more attractive: it saves 2补给/turn = 11.6金/turn, and my inputs (1粮+1矿) are worth only 3.8金 at depressed prices. Net saving ~8金/turn (if prices stay low) or ~5.6金/turn at baseline.\n\nCost: 200金+12木 (平原). I have 74金, 4木.\n\nAlso — arbitrage idea: buy food at 1.0 (cheap) and use it in 补给厂. Food 1.0 → converts with 矿 2.8 into 补给 at 5.8 each. That's a strong arbitrage. 补给厂 needs 1粮+1矿 per turn; I produce 4粮+2矿 per turn. So I can run it at 2补给/turn from own production, and even buy extra food/ore to... no, the factory is capped at 1粮+1矿 input per turn (produces 2补给).\n\nHmm, so one 补给厂 covers 2 of my 3 armies' needs. Saves 11.6金/turn. That's huge relative to my income.\n\nSo: PRIORITY = 补给厂 (200金+12木).\n\nSecond: stop selling food (price 1.0, worthless). Actually, since 补给厂 consumes food, my food production becomes an input, not a dump product. \n\nLet me revise: \n- Build 补给厂 at 达川 or 新丘 (平原, 200金+12木). Needs 1电 (grid 产2/需1 → 需2 ✓ exactly balanced).\n\nCareful: grid 产2/需2 is exactly balanced — if the 能源厂's wood supply runs out, everything stops. 木材能源厂 consumes 1木/turn. I produce 4木/turn. Fine.\n\n- Then 黄金矿场.\n\nCash: 74. Need 200. Gap 126. Income: sell 木4/turn (1.8 = 7金), 矿2/turn (2.8 = 5.6), 粮 (keep for factory). So ~12金/turn net after 补给 purchases (17/turn)... negative!\n\nUgh. 补给 purchases eat everything.\n\nHmm, but wait: I can reduce 补给 buying by letting the warehouse dip. Let me think about the real budget:\n- Outflow: 3补给/turn = 17.4金 at 5.8\n- Inflow: sell 木4 (7.2) + 矿2 (5.6) = 12.8金; food 4/turn worthless at 1.0 (4金)\n- Net: -0.6 to +4.6金/turn\n\nSo I cannot save 126金. Dead end!\n\nTherefore I MUST reduce army upkeep. This is now clear: 3 armies at 17.4金/turn vs my ~13-17金/turn gross production. The army is eating the entire economy.\n\nOptions:\n(1) Kill one army (starve) → upkeep 11.6金/turn. Net +2 to +6. Still barely.\n(2) Kill two armies → upkeep 5.8. Net +7 to +12. Then 补给厂 in ~15 turns.\n(3) Build 补给厂 first — but can't afford.\n\nHmm, what if I sell MORE stock? I have 6 ore (17金), 4 wood (7金), 4 food (4金). Total ~28金 liquidation. Not enough.\n\nLet me reconsider: is there a cheaper path to income? \n\nAH WAIT. Important idea: **sell 装备? No, 0.** \n\n**What about buying food at 1.0 and... no sink.**\n\nHmm, let me reconsider 黄金矿场: 300金 → 10金/turn. Also unaffordable.\n\nOK, so what's the actual best move? Let me think about the \"starve armies\" option seriously.\n\nIf I stop buying 补给 entirely:\n- Warehouse 4 → covers T14 (3), leaving 1.\n- T15: 1 → covers 1 army, other 2 starve (-10HP each).\n- Then armies at 98/90/90 etc. They lose 10HP/turn each.\n- They die in ~9-10 turns.\n- Cost: 0金/turn.\n- Result: I lose 3 armies (180金 of recruitment) and my military.\n\nThat's too destructive. But partial: let exactly ONE army starve (the weakest) and keep buying 2/turn for the other two.\n\nHmm, but the warehouse is shared — I can't choose which army eats. Presumably it draws from the warehouse and any army without supply starves. I can't control which.\n\nActually, I could deliberately not buy enough: buy 2/turn. Then 1 army starves each turn. Over 10 turns the weakest dies. Then I'm at 2 armies and buy 2/turn.\n\nCost of transition: ~10 turns where one army is at reduced HP (dies eventually). Saves 5.8金/turn after that.\n\nHmm, is that worth it? Losing army #1 (98HP) = 60金 sunk. Saving 5.8金/turn from T25 onward... over 40 turns = 232金.