ow baseline. That means the whole market is flooded. 楚 and 齐 are producing and selling. Prices regress toward baseline each turn though. So next turn food might be 1.2, wood 1.85, ore 3.0.\n\nIf prices recover to baseline (2/2/4), my gross = 8+8+8 = 24金/turn. Minus 17.4 upkeep = +6.6. Minus 11.6 (2 armies) = +12.4金/turn. 补给厂 in 10 turns.\n\nSo: (1) cut to 2 armies' feeding, (2) wait for price recovery, (3) build 补给厂, (4) then 黄金矿场, (5) then re-expand with the 2 armies (still 100 dmg → plains/desert tiles in 1 round).\n\nHmm, but deliberately starving an army... Let me reconsider: is there any chance 楚/齐 attack me in the next 20 turns? They're 15-20 tiles away. To invade, they'd need armies with 补给 lines. Extremely costly. Risk is low.\n\nAlso, my armies are inland at 绥郡 — no threat.\n\nAlternatively, a gentler approach: **walk the armies home and just accept slow savings**? Upkeep continues regardless.\n\nHmm, let me reconsider ONE more option: **sell 装备? no. Buy cheap food at 1.0 to feed... no.**\n\nOK, what about this: **the 3rd army's value** — with 3 armies I take 1 tile/turn. Each tile is a lottery for 黄金/石油. 绥郡 gave 石油1 (worth 6金/turn developed). 珍崖 gave 矿3 (12金/turn developed). So tiles ARE valuable — but only once developed, which needs cash.\n\nDecision: I'll reduce to 2 armies by under-feeding (buy 2/turn), and use the freed cash to reach 补给厂. Meanwhile keep the 2 armies to grab 1 plains/desert tile per turn? With 2 armies: 100 dmg vs 100HP plains 野人 → dies exactly, my armies take 50/2 = 25 each. Then heal 25. So attack every other turn. Hills/forests not viable.\n\nHmm, actually wait. Let me reconsider: maybe DON'T starve an army. Instead, let me check: is 补给 consumption really 1/army/turn even when not at war? Yes.\n\nAlright, alternative that avoids destroying an army: **build 补给厂 as fast as possible by liquidating everything and NOT buying 补给 for 2 turns (letting armies take -10HP each)**.\n\n- T14: warehouse 4. T15: 1. T16: 0 → all 3 starve (-10 each). T17: buy 3.\n- Savings: ~17金 over 2 turns. Armies at 78/80/80. Not dead.\n- This is a \"buffer dip\" tactic. But it doesn't solve the structural problem.\n\nStructural: income 13-24, upkeep 17.4. \n\nHmm, let me look at it from a different angle: **increase income by developing cheap buildings with my own wood**. I have 4木 and produce 4/turn. A 矿场 at 珍崖 (沙漠) = 112金+5木. A 矿场 at 沃坝... at cap. A 农场 at 碧岭 = 60金+5木 → 2金/turn (at 1.0 food price, useless!).\n\nFood at 1.0 → farms are worthless now. Ore at 2.8 → mines give 2.8金/turn for 112金 = 40回合. Bad.\n\nGold mine: 10金/turn fixed, 300金 = 30回合. Best.\n\nSo the gold mine is the only good investment, and prices need to recover for anything else.\n\nFINAL DECISION for T14 onward:\n1. Stop expanding (armies idle → they heal to 100 and just cost 补给).\n   Hmm, idle armies cost 17.4/turn for nothing. That's the worst.\n   \n   Actually no — let me use them! Since upkeep is paid regardless, grabbing tiles is \"free\" incremental value. The marginal cost of an attack is just HP (which heals). So I SHOULD keep attacking while I'm paying for 3 armies anyway!\n   \n   Yes! That's right: the 补给 is a sunk per-turn cost. Once I've decided to keep 3 armies, I should extract maximum value = grab as many tiles as possible.\n\n2. So: keep attacking 1 tile/turn (P/D/F/H all feasible with 3 armies), while prices recover, and build the gold mine when affordable.\n\nBut cash for the gold mine is the problem. Hmm.\n\nOK, compromise: Continue attacking (sunk cost), and funnel every spare gold toward 补给厂 (which cuts the upkeep by 11.6金/turn, the single biggest lever).\n\nTo reach 200金: sell stock gradually as prices recover.\n\nCurrent: 74金. Need 126 more. \n- Sell 矿 6 as price recovers: ~20金\n- Sell 木 4: ~8金\n- Production sales: ~13-24金/turn gross, minus 17 upkeep.\n\nRealistically 补给厂 around T20-22. That's OK-ish.\n\nHmm, alternatively: let me consider selling food at 1.0 — no, that's value destruction.\n\nActually here's a thought: I have 4粮 stock and produce 4/turn = 8粮 by T15. Food at 1.0 is worthless. But 补给厂 converts food+ore into 补给 at 5.8. So the factory makes my food valuable. Circular.\n\nLet me also consider buying food at 1.0 to stockpile for the factory? Factory caps at 1粮/turn input. No benefit.\n\nOK. Let me also reconsider: maybe build the 补给厂 at 珍崖/绥郡 (沙漠 ×1.4 = 280金)? No, build on plains (达川 or 新丘 or 碧岭) = 200金.\n\nAlright, T14 remaining actions:\n- Buy 补给 2 (12金) → 62金. Warehouse 6 → covers T15.\n  Actually warehouse 4, need 3 this turn → 1 left. Buy 2 → 6 → after T14 = 3, T15 = 0. Hmm. Let me buy 3 (17.4) → 7 → covers T15 fully, T16 partially.\n  \nHmm, buying at 5.8 is expensive; price will regress. Buy 2 now (12金).\n\n- Should I attack? Armies are at 绥郡(18,9) at full HP. Adjacent: (17,9)F, (17,10)P, (18,10)H, (19,10)H, (20,9)H, (19,9)✓沃坝, (17,8)✓永湾, (18,8)✓霜塘.\n  (17,10)P is plains — easiest! 150 dmg vs 100 → 1 round, take 17 each.\n  Let me take (17,10)P.\n\nActually hold on, is grabbing more tiles really good given I can't develop them? Each tile adds ~20 slots and some resources. Undeveloped tiles produce nothing. So they're pure future optionality. They cost nothing extra (armies already paid). So yes, grab them.\n\nBut HP: if armies die, I lose 60金 each and expansion stops. Take care.\n\nLet me attack (17,10)P.\n\nHmm, wait: after (17,10), from there: (16,9)P, (16,10), (17,9)F, (18,10)H, (18,9)✓. Good chain.\n\nLet me do: attack (17,10) + buy 补给 2.\n\nCash: 74 - 12 = 62.\n\nLet me go.",
