            "content": "第15回合判断：我12块地已有约20个农场位+4矿位+1金1油，**可开发容量远超我的资金**——所以再占地本身不再增加价值，现金才是瓶颈。但攻击野人零金币支出（只掉血、和平期免费回血），所以维持\"一回合一格\"继续吞地摊薄已付的补给费，同时把补给买量压到最低。\n\n",
            "reasoning_content": "Turn 15. Treasury 62, food 8, wood 7, ore 8, supply 3 (3 armies consume 3/turn → runs out now).\n\nArmies all at 100HP at 武州 (17,10).\n\n12 tiles. Prices all 贱 except 装备/补给.\n\nKey: 武州 (17,10) has 耕地4! That's a lot.\n\nPriorities:\n1. Buy 补给 (3 needed, price 5.7 = 17金). Treasury 62 → 45.\n2. Attack: from 武州(17,10), adjacent: (17,11)P, (16,10)H, (16,11)D, (18,11)H, (18,10)H, (17,9)F, (16,9)P, (18,9)✓绥郡.\n   Best: (17,11)P plains (150 dmg, 1 round, take 17 each) or (16,9)P or (16,11)D.\n   Let me take (17,11)P — plains, likely 耕地.\n   \n   Hmm, or should I stop expanding and consolidate? Let me think about the marginal value again.\n   \n   Actually, here's a thought I should weigh: 武州 has 耕地4. If I develop it (4 farms = 240金+20木 → 4粮/turn = 8金/turn at baseline), payback 30 turns. Undeveloped tiles give nothing.\n   \n   My cash is 62. I can't develop. So more tiles = more unbuilt optionality. Marginal value declining.\n   \n   BUT: the armies cost 17金/turn regardless. Using them to grab a tile each turn is \"free\" in the sense that the cost is already sunk. However, HP risk exists (17 per attack, heals 25 when at peace). Since they're at 100 and attacks cost 17, they can attack ~5 times then need rest. So sustainably ~1 tile per 1.5-2 turns.\n\n   Actually attack every turn: -17/turn, no healing (in combat). After 5 turns they're at 15. Then rest 3-4 turns to heal. So pattern: 5 attack, 4 rest → 5 tiles / 9 turns.\n   \n   Hmm, that's fine.\n\n3. Should I sell anything? All prices 贱 (粮1.2, 木1.8, 矿2.8). Ore at 2.8 vs baseline 4.0 is the biggest discount → hold ore. Wood 1.8 vs 2.0 → nearly baseline, mild discount. Food 1.2 vs 2.0 → deep discount.\n   \n   I need cash though. Selling 木 3 at 1.8 = 5.4金. Meh.\n   \n   Actually, here's the thing: I MUST accumulate 200金 for 补给厂. My income sources:\n   - Sell production: 木4 (7.2), 矿2 (5.6), 粮4 (4.8 at 1.2) = 17.6金/turn gross\n   - Buy 补给: -17金/turn\n   - Net: +0.6金/turn\n   \n   That's a dead end. I cannot save anything at 3 armies.\n   \n   So the ONLY escape is: reduce army count OR build 补给厂.\n   \n   Since 补给厂 needs 200金 which I can't save... \n   \n   Hmm, wait. What if I liquidate stock? I have 8粮(9.6) + 7木(12.6) + 8矿(22.4) = 44.6金 total stock. Plus 62 cash = 107. Not 200.\n\n   What if I sell everything (44.6) → 107金, then... still need 93 more.\n   \n   Hmm. What if I let ONE army die? Then upkeep = 11.6/turn, income 17.6 → net +6/turn. 补给厂 in ~15 turns. Ugh.\n   \n   What if I let TWO armies die? upkeep 5.8 → net +11.8/turn. 补给厂 in ~12 turns. But then only 1 army (can't take any tile alone).\n   \n   Alternatively: **sell stock + don't buy 补给 for 2 turns + build 补给厂 at ~T18**. Let me compute:\n   - T15: sell 矿8 (22金, crashes ore to ~2.5) hmm.\n   \n   Actually, let me reconsider: maybe I'm wrong that I can't save. Let me reconsider whether to buy 补给 at 5.7 or let armies go hungry occasionally.\n   \n   Starving costs -10HP/army/turn. Armies at 100HP. If I skip 补给 purchases for 3 turns, all 3 armies drop to 70. That \"saves\" 51金. Then they'd need healing (25/turn, 2 turns at peace). This is a way to convert HP into gold. HP regenerates for free at peace!\n   \n   So: starving an army for 1 turn = -10HP, which heals in 0.4 turns of peace. So the \"cost\" of skipping 补给 is just tempo, not permanent loss (as long as HP doesn't hit 0).\n   \n   That means: I can skip 补给 purchases when armies are at high HP, and only buy when they're low! Effectively, armies can run on \"HP buffer.\"\n   \n   Optimal: keep armies at 100HP by buying 补给 only... no wait. If I never buy 补给, armies lose 10HP/turn and die at 0. HP regen only happens when supplied (\"非交战且补给够时每回合回血+25\"). So unsupplied armies don't regen — they just decay.\n   \n   Right: \"断粮则-10HP可能饿毙\". And regen requires 补给够. So the HP buffer is one-directional: you can bank ~100HP of starvation = 10 turns of free upkeep for 1 army. But eventually they die.\n   \n   So starving = slow death of armies