            "reasoning_content": "End turn. \n\nNext turn: I need to think about the structural cash problem. Let me consider a decisive move: sell all stock (粮8 + 木7 + 矿8 = 9.6 + 12.6 + 22.4 = 44.6金) to get to ~85金, and... still not 200.\n\nHmm. Let me think about the \"starve one army\" plan more concretely, since it's the structural fix.\n\nActually — better idea! What about **moving the armies home to rest and stop attacking**, thereby... no, upkeep continues.\n\nHmm, what about this: I could deliberately march an army into a 山地 野人 tile alone → it dies in 2 rounds (dealing 25/round, taking 50/round: 100HP → 50 → 0). Cost: nothing extra (补给 already paid). Benefit: permanent 5.7金/turn saving.\n\nThat's actually the FASTEST way to reduce upkeep: 2 turns instead of 10.\n\nIs it worth it? Losing 1 army (60金 sunk) to save 5.7金/turn × remaining turns. If the game runs 40 more turns = 228金. Definitely worth it economically.\n\nBut with 2 armies (100 dmg) I can still take plains/desert tiles in 1 round (exactly 100 = 100HP → dies, my armies take 25 each). And 2 armies at 100HP with 25 damage per attack → 4 attacks then rest. Fine.\n\nHmm, but do I even need to take more tiles? I concluded territory isn't my bottleneck. So reducing to 2 armies (or even 1) is economically optimal.\n\nLet me reconsider: 1 army = 5.7/turn upkeep, net income +11.9/turn (current prices). 补给厂 in ~13 turns (from 45金 + stock 45 = 90 → need 110 more → 9 turns). \n2 armies: net +6.2 → 补给厂 in ~25 turns.\n3 armies: net +0.6 → never.\n\nSo going to 1 army is much better economically! But 1 army = no expansion capability at all (can't take a tile alone).\n\nHmm, but I don't need expansion.\n\nTrade-off: lose 2 armies (120金 sunk) to save 11.4金/turn.\n\nBut wait — there's a catch: with 1 army I also can't defend if anything happens. And 武州 耕4 etc. need no defense.\n\nHmm, let me be moderate: reduce to 2 armies. Net +6.2/turn at current prices, +14/turn at baseline. 补给厂 in ~10-15 turns. Then with 补给厂, upkeep drops to ~6/turn for 2 armies (factory covers 2 of 2... wait, factory produces 2补给/turn, 2 armies need 2/turn → FULLY covered!). Then upkeep = 1粮+1矿/turn (internal, ~6.8金 opportunity cost) and zero 补给 purchases.\n\nWith 3 armies, factory covers 2, still buy 1/turn.\n\nSo 2 armies + 补给厂 = fully self-sufficient supply! That's a nice end state: income 24金/turn gross - 0 purchases = strong.\n\nOK so: reduce to 2 armies, save for 补给厂.\n\nHow to reduce: send army #3 alone into 山地 (17,6)M or (19,5)M... those are far from 武州(17,10). Nearest 山地: (17,6)M — distance from (17,10) is 4. Too far to walk (each move costs... free actually, movement is free apart from 补给).\n\nHmm, simpler: just stop buying 3/turn and buy 2/turn. The engine will starve one army. It decays 10HP/turn and dies in 10 turns. During which it still can't fight well.\n\nOr: march one army to a mountain and suicide it. (19,5)M is 4 tiles from 武州. Walking there takes 4 turns (1 tile/turn), costing 补给... and it would need to be alone.\n\nHonestly the simplest: buy 2/turn and let the game pick. Actually — I worry the starvation might hit a random army and the \"fed\" ones stay at 100. Over 10 turns one dies. That's fine, and I save 5.7×10 = 57金 in the process.\n\nHmm, but there's a risk: if all 3 armies are at, say, 70 and I then buy 3/turn, they heal. The starvation isn't targeted.\n\nLet me just do it: buy 2/turn for the next ~5 turns (saving ~5.7/turn = 28金), and see what happens. Actually, let me be more decisive: I'll send one army away to be a \"raider\" and let it starve deliberately? Too fiddly.\n\nSIMPLEST DECISIVE ACTION: Stop buying 补给 for 3-4 turns (save ~23金), let all 3 armies drop to ~65-70, then buy 2/turn permanently (covering 2 armies, third decays to death over 7 turns).\n\nHmm, that's messy. Let me reconsider ONE more time...\n\nActually, you know what? Let me reconsider the premise. Is 补给 really needed? What if I just... let me re-read: \"补给厂(粮1+矿1→补给2)\"; \"补给仓每军每回合耗1（骑兵2），空则军队挨饿\". And market 补给 5金.\n\nYes. 3 armies = 15金/turn at baseline. My gross production at baseline = 24金/turn.\n\nSo armies eat 62% of gross income at baseline.\n\nHmm OK. So the answer is clear: fewer armies.\n\nLet me also double check: is my read right that developing tiles requires 2540金? Yes, roughly.\n\nSo: 2 armies it is. And I'll get there by under-buying 补给.\n\nFor now (T15 done): end turn. T16: buy 2 补给 (or 0 if warehouse OK), sell a bit of wood.\n\nActually, let me reconsider whether to instead keep 3 armies and go for a bigger gamble: use them to grab 5-6 more tiles quickly, hoping for 黄金. A 黄金矿场 site on plains = 200金 for +10金/turn. Hmm.\n\nNo. Let me be disciplined: economy first.\n\nLet me end the turn.",
