            "reasoning_content": "Turn 21. Situation:\n- 国库44, 粮22, 木17, 矿5, 补给仓0, 3 armies all at 100HP at 朔观(14,13).\n- Note: 补给仓 0! Last turn I bought 3, warehouse became 3, then 3 armies consumed 3 → 0. And \"上一回合结算: 军队3支, 补给仓0\" — no starvation message this time? The 近讯 shows 断粮 at T19 but not T20. So at T20 they were fed (3 bought, 3 consumed).\n\nNow warehouse 0 → this turn, if I don't buy, all 3 starve (-10HP each).\n\nArmies are at (14,13) — far west at column 14. That's 8 tiles from my core (19,8). Note: they're deep in my own territory chain (14,13)→(15,12)→(16,11)→(17,11)→... all mine. So supply lines are fine (my tiles).\n\nHmm, wait. Actually armies consume 补给 from the national warehouse regardless of location. OK.\n\nKey decision: my plan says cut to 2 armies. So buy 2 补给 → 1 army starves.\n\nBut note the armies are all at 100HP now. If I buy 2, one starves (-10 → 90).\n\nAlso: should I attack? My 国策 says fill gaps near core: (17,9)F, (16,9)P, (16,7)P, (20,6)P, (20,5)P, (18,5)F. But armies are at (14,13), far from those. Marching them back takes ~5-8 turns of walking (free, but 补给 consumption continues).\n\nHmm! That's an important point: the armies are deep in the west at (14,13). To grab the gap tiles near my core they'd need to march back ~5-6 turns. Meanwhile they eat 3 补给/turn = 17.4金/turn.\n\nAlternatively, keep grabbing tiles in the west (adjacent to (14,13)): (13,12)P, (13,13)M, (13,14)H, (14,11)P, (14,12)M, (14,14)H, (15,11)H, (15,13)F, (15,14)M, (15,10)P.\n\nHmm, but my 国策 says stop deep expansion.\n\nLet me reconsider: what's the best use of these armies right now, given they cost 17.4金/turn?\n\nOption A: March them home (to the core, ~5 turns), then use 2 of them to fill gaps. Cost: 5 turns × 17.4 = 87金, no tiles gained.\n\nOption B: Keep grabbing western tiles (1/turn) until army #3 dies, then march the remaining 2 home. Each tile = future development optionality.\n\nOption C: Grab tiles that connect back to core along a useful line.\n\nHmm. Actually, let me reconsider the whole thing. The real issue: I'm at 44金 and my 补给厂 goal is 200金. I need ~156金. My net savings rate is ~0 at 3 armies, ~4/turn at 2 armies.\n\nSo: cut to 2 armies ASAP, then save.\n\nAnd while cutting, use the 3rd army's remaining HP to grab tiles (free).\n\nBut the armies are far west. Let me have them grab a few more western tiles while #3 decays, then march home.\n\nActually — here's a cleaner idea: **let the armies march west taking tiles, and eventually I'll walk them back**. Or better: since they need to come home anyway, have them take tiles ON THE WAY home. From (14,13), a route home through my territory: (15,12)→(16,11)→(17,10)→... all already mine. So they'd pass through my own tiles.\n\nAlternatively they could take (15,10)P, (16,9)P, (17,9)F, (18,9)... wait (18,9) is 绥郡 (mine). So a diagonal chain back east: (14,13)→(15,12)✓mine→(16,11)✓mine→(17,10)✓mine→...\n\nHmm, so going home passes through my own tiles. To grab tiles on the way, they'd take (15,13)F or (15,14)M etc.\n\nLet me reconsider: which tiles are most valuable to grab?\n- (16,9)P: fills a gap between 永湾(17,8), 珍崖(18,6)... it's adjacent to 武州(17,10) and 永湾(17,8). Plains, likely 耕地. Good.\n- (17,9)F: forest gap right in the middle of my core (between 永湾, 武州, 绥郡, 凝岭, 霜塘). Fills a hole. Good.\n- (16,7)P: adjacent to 珍崖(18,6)? no, distance 2. Adjacent to (17,8)永湾 ✓.\n- (20,6)P, (20,5)P, (18,5)F, (17,5)P: northern.\n\nSo the gap-filling targets are all near the core (16-20, 5-10), which is 5-7 tiles from (14,13).\n\nMarching there takes 5-7 turns × 17.4 = 87-122金. That's a lot.\n\nAlternative: just leave the armies where they are and grab adjacent tiles (cheap, no movement cost), then decide.\n\nHmm, honestly: given my cash crisis, maybe the best move is to grab 1 tile/turn adjacent to their current position while #3 decays, then march the 2 survivors home.\n\nActually, movement is free (only 补给 consumption, which happens regardless). So marching home costs the same as attacking. Attacking gains a tile. So attack!\n\nLet me attack from (14,13): adjacent wild options: (13,12)P, (13,13)M, (13,14)H, (14,11)P, (14,12)M, (14,14)H, (15,11)H, (15,13)F, (15,14)M.\n\nBest: plains (14,11)P or (13,12)P, or forest (15,13)F.\n- (14,11)P: plains, adjacent to 静里(16,11)? no, distance 2. Adjacent to (15,10)P, (15,11)H, (15,12)凝浦✓, (13,12)P.\n- (13,12)P: adjacent to (14,13)✓.\n\nHmm, these extend west into a cul-de-sac. My 国策 says don't go past column 14. We're at 14.\n\nLet me instead consider: (15,13)F (forest, adjacent to 朔观(14,13) ✓ and 凝浦(15,12) ✓). Forest with 3 armies: 150×0.9 = 135 > 100 ✓ 1 round.\n\nOr (15,11)H (hills): 150×0.75 = 112 > 100 ✓ 1 round.\n\nHmm. Let me pick (15,13)F — it's on the eastern side, closer to home direction, and forest gives 木头.\n\nActually wait. Let me reconsider the whole army question once more.\n\nHonest assessment: 3 armies cost 17.4金/turn. My income is ~17金/turn. I'm at 44金.\n\nIf I want the 补给厂 (200金), I need to save 156金. At 2 armies with income 17 - upkeep 11.6 = +5.4/turn → 29 turns. At baseline prices (income 24) → +12.4/turn → 13 turns.\n\nHmm. Prices are recovering as I stop dumping (粮 1.1→1.2, 木 1.7, 矿 2.6 — actually still falling/slowly rising).\n\nAlternatively: **sell the wood stockpile**. 17木 at 1.7 = 28.9金. That's 5 turns of savings. And I need 12木 for the 补给厂... Hmm.\n\nActually here's a cleaner idea I keep dancing around: **sell wood (my most abundant, least-depressed surplus) to fund the 补给厂 faster**. I produce 4木/turn and only need ~5木 per building occasionally. Wood at 1.7 vs baseline 2.0 = only 15% discount (vs food 40%, ore 35%).\n\nLet me sell 8木 now (+13.6) → 58金. Keep 9木 + 4/turn.\n\nAnd buy 2 补给 (11.6) → 46金. Warehouse 2 → feeds 2 armies, 1 starves.\n\nHmm, and attack (15,13)F.\n\nLet me reconsider: should I attack at all? If I attack, all 3 armies take 17 damage and don't heal. The 2 fed ones would be at 83, the unfed at 73. Then next turn, if I rest: fed heal to 100, unfed... hmm, \"非交战且补给够时\" heals. So the unfed one doesn't heal.\n\nActually, maybe I should NOT attack and instead march them home? Marching also means no healing (mv isn't combat though — they'd still be at peace, so they'd heal). Hmm, mv + heal both possible? \"非交战且补给够时每回合回血+25HP\" — yes, marching armies are at peace so they heal.\n\nSo: march home + heal + starve #3. That gets the 2 good armies to the core where I want them, and #3 dies.\n\nHmm, but that forgoes tiles.\n\nLet me think about what's actually best. Honestly, at this point:\n- More tiles have low value (I can't develop them).\n- Getting armies home matters for defending the core & filling gaps later.\n- #3 must die to cut costs.\n\nActually, you know what? Let me reconsider ONE more time whether to keep 3 armies... no. Cut.\n\nDECISION for T21:\n1. Attack (15,13)F with 3 armies — gains a tile (forest, 木头), and #3's decay doesn't matter since it's dying anyway. Wait, but if I attack, the 2 good armies take 17 damage. They're at 100 → 83. Then next turn rest → 100. Fine.\n\nHmm, but actually attacking means they stay at (15,13), still far west.\n\nAlternatively: attack (15,13)F now, then (15,12)... that's mine. Hmm, from (15,13) the next wild tiles toward home: (16,13)H, (16,14)?, (15,14)M, (14,14)H.\n\n(16,13)H: hills, adjacent to (15,13) ✓. 150×0.75 = 112 > 100 ✓.\n\nSo they could chain: (15,13)F → (16,13)H → (17,13)H → (17,12)H → ... that's a southern/eastern route back toward the core! And it grabs 3-4 tiles along the way.\n\nActually (17,12)H is adjacent to 翠仓(17,11)✓ and 朔观... and (17,13)H adjacent to (16,13)H ✓ and (18,12)M.\n\nHmm, this route goes through hills which are +25% defense — with 3 armies (112 dmg) it's a 1-round kill but tight. With 2 armies (75 dmg) it's NOT enough. So hills must be taken while #3 lives.\n\nLet me plan the march: T21 (15,13)F, T22 (16,13)H, T23 (17,13)H, T24 (17,12)H, T25 (16,10)H or (18,12)M...\n\nHmm, this is a nice \"grab tiles on the way home\" route. But hills with 2 armies after #3 dies would take 2 rounds.\n\nOK, let me just do T21: attack (15,13)F, buy 2 补给, sell 8 木.\n\nCash: 44 + 13.6 - 11.6 = 46.\n\nHmm, wait: 木头 1.7 is 贱 (my 国策 says don't sell below 1.9). Ugh. But I need cash. Let me sell only 5木 (+8.5) → 41 - 11.6 = ...\n\nHmm, let me reconsider. Actually, my 国策 discipline says don't sell below thresholds. But I'm at 44金 which is above the 30 red line. Let me hold wood this turn and just buy 2 补给.\n\nCash: 44 - 11.6 = 32.4. That's near the red line.\n\nHmm. Risky. Let me sell 5 木 (+8.5) → 40.6 - 11.6 = 29.\n\nAlternatively buy 1 补给 and let 2 armies starve? No — I want to keep 2 healthy.\n\nHmm, actually, wait. Let me reconsider: if I'm cutting to 2 armies anyway, and #3 will die, maybe I should just NOT attack (save all HP) and buy 2 补给. The armies at 100/100/100. #3 starves: 90, 80, 70... dies at 0 → 10 turns.\n\nActually, #3 at 100HP starving = 10 turns of \"free\" existence. During which it contributes 50 damage to attacks. So attacking while it starves is efficient.\n\nBut attacks cost the good armies 17HP each (which then need 补给+time to heal). Hmm, healing is free (just needs 补给, which they consume anyway).\n\nSo: attack every other turn. T21 attack, T22 rest, T23 attack...\n\nLet me simplify: T21 attack (15,13)F, buy 2 补给, sell 5 木 to stay above the red line.\n\nActually, let me reconsider selling wood once more. Wood 1.7, baseline 2.0. I hold 17 and produce 4/turn. My wood needs: 补给厂 12, 黄金矿场 10, 石油厂 8 each. So I'll need ~30-40 wood over the next 20 turns, and I produce 4/turn = 80 over 20 turns. So I have a big wood surplus. Selling 5-8 is fine.\n\nThe loss vs baseline: 0.3 × 8 = 2.4金. Trivial. Cash in hand is worth more (it compounds via buildings).\n\nLet me sell 8 木 (+13.6).\n\nFinal T21: attack (15,13)F, buy 补给 2, sell 木头 8.\n\nCash: 44 + 13.6 - 11.6 = 46.\n\nLet's go.",
