            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "",
            "reasoning_content": "Let me analyze the situation. I'm Chu, turn 1. Treasury 1500 gold, food 20, wood 60, ore 10, oil 0, equipment 5, supplies 10. 5 tiles, no buildings, no army. 16 adjacent wasteland tiles, all defended by primitives (100 HP each).\n\nLet me think about the game mechanics. I need to check rules for building costs and combat. Let me query rules first.\n\nKey considerations:\n1. Building economy: costs, income. Let me check econ panel to see profitability.\n2. Expansion: need army to take tiles from primitives.\n3. Diplomacy: Qin and Qi are neutral.\n\nPlan: Build resource buildings first (林场, 农场, 矿场), then 兵营 requires 3 buildings on that tile. Then recruit army, attack primitives to expand.\n\nLet me check the rules and econ first.\n\nLet me call query with res/econ/land/army... Actually econ panel gives building economics. Let's do rules() and econ() in parallel.",
