            "reasoning_content": "秦 is at (17-21, 6-10) — far northwest of me (27-30, 22-26). Distance ~8-10 tiles. No conflict in the near term; they have no army yet, 457 gold (spent more than me), and are building lumber/mines. They also have a 木材能源厂 at 朔原 with 3 slots used — likely building a barracks next turn (needs 3 buildings — they have it!). So 秦 could recruit an army at turn 5-6 too.\n\nTheir territory: 2 mines at 沃坝 (mountain), lots of wood. They're investing in ore/wood.\n\nNow, my turn 4 actions:\n1. Build 兵营 at 碧庭 (350金+20木). Wood: I have 15, need 20 + 15 for 能源厂 = 35. So buy ~20-25 wood. Wood price 2.5 (high). Buying 25 wood at ~2.5-2.8 = ~68金. Hmm.\n\nAlternative: build 兵营 only this turn (20木 → need to buy 5-10 wood), and build 能源厂 next turn. But then 兵营 completes T5 without power → 停摆, can't recruit. Timeline: 兵营 T4 build → active T5; 能源厂 T4 build → active T5 → recruit T5. If 能源厂 built T5 → active T6 → recruit T6. One turn delay costs 1 turn of expansion. Cash: 805 - 350(兵营) - 68(wood) - 120(能源厂) = 267. That's low but I have 26 food, 12 ore, 5 equipment, 10 supplies — plenty of material to convert. And I can sell food/ore at need.\n\nActually, wait. Consider: 兵营 requires 1电 to function. 能源厂 2电. Also I want 补给厂 (1电) soon. So 2 能源厂 eventually. Each 能源厂 burns 1 wood/turn; my lumber income is 4/turn (岚栅2, 苍堰1, 宣邑1) → after 2 能源厂, net 2 wood/turn for construction. Hmm, that's slow; I'd need to buy wood regularly (cheap: 2-2.5/wood = 5 gold per building's wood... fine).\n\nLet me decide: build both 兵营 (碧庭) and 木材能源厂 (云谷? or 苍堰?) this turn, buying 25 wood.\n\nWhere to put 能源厂? Any tile. Put it at 苍堰 (plain, near center) or 宣邑. Let me put it at 苍堰 (27,24) — plain, no resource dependency. Actually careful: 能源厂 doesn't consume local resources, it's \"任地可建\". Choose a tile that has limited resource value for other buildings, e.g., 岚栅 (耕1木2, has 2 lumber already, 3 slots... 岚栅 capacity: 2 lumber + 1 farm = 3 buildings max, then it's full; adding 能源厂 makes 4). Hmm, for 市政厅 later I want a tile with many buildings — 碧庭 is the hub (5 farms + barracks = 6 → 市政厅 eligible at T5!). Nice: 碧庭 will have 6 slots used after 兵营 (3 farms + barracks = 4). Wait, 3 farms + 1 barracks = 4 slots. Need 6 for 市政厅. 碧庭 capacity: 5 farms + 2 lumber = 7 + barracks = 8. So 碧庭 could reach 6-7 slots by T7 and then 市政厅 (500金) — probably too expensive later. Skip for now.\n\nPut 能源厂 at 宣邑 (28,23): 宣邑 has 矿场+林场 = 2 slots, plain. Fine. Or 苍堰. Either. I'll use 苍堰 (27,24) plain.\n\nHmm, actually location matters for nothing except adjacency-based attacks; power is national. Let's use 宣邑 to spread buildings.\n\n2. Should I also build anything else? Cash after: 805 - 350 - 120 - 68(wood) = 267. Tight. Nothing else.\n\nWait, actually maybe I should sell some stuff to raise cash: food price 2.1 (slightly high), I have 26 food and will need 10/army. Ore price 3.4 (below baseline 4) — bad time to sell. Equipment 8.1 — I have exactly 5 for the first recruit.\n\nLet me sell 10 food at 2.1 → ~21 gold, price drops slightly. That helps a bit. Actually, food is needed for recruiting (10/army) and for 补给厂 (1 food → 2 supply). Selling food then buying back later at higher price is silly. But my farm income is 4/turn, so I'll produce plenty. Let me hold for now and sell surplus later.\n\nBuy wood: 25 wood at 2.5 → the buy pushes price up; total cost maybe 65-70. Let me buy 25.\n\nActually, let me compute more carefully: I need 20木 (兵营) + 15木 (能源厂) = 35, have 15, plus income +4 wood at settlement (end of turn, after building? Building consumes now; income at settlement). So I need 20 now → buy 20 wood (cost ~50-55), leaving 0 wood, then settlement +4 wood. Hmm, that's fine but let me buy 25 for a small buffer.\n\n3. Spy on 齐? 100金. 秦 report showed they're far away and not a threat. 齐's location unknown — could be to my east/south. Knowing whether 齐 is near my expansion direction has value... but 100金 when I'd have ~150 left after builds. Hmm. Risky. But the info mainly m