            "reasoning_content": "Turn 5: The 兵营 and 能源厂 are now built (碧庭 shows 兵营×1, 宣邑 shows 木材能源厂×1). Grid shows 产0/需0 — meaning it's computed at settlement? It says 电网 产0/需0 正常. Hmm, that's the current state before production. At settlement, 能源厂 produces 2电 (burning 1 wood), 兵营 needs 1电.\n\nNow recruit 1 infantry: costs 10粮 + 5装. I have 31粮, 5装. \n\nThen I have 1 army at 碧庭. Can't attack safely alone. Options:\n- Recruit now (army #1), and next turn buy equipment for army #2.\n- Cash: 263. Equipment 5 = ~41 gold.\n\nAlso consider: attack with 1 army at 25% risk? Let's compute the combat math more carefully. \"每军基础伤害 50，受守方地形+城堡防御%修正…总伤害分摊\". So in a battle at 碧庭-adjacent plain (29,23) with 1 primitive (100HP, def 0%):\n- My army deals 50 → primitive takes 50 (split among 1 enemy = all 50).\n- Primitive deals 50 → my army takes 50.\nAfter round 1: my army 50HP, primitive 50HP.\nRound 2 (next turn, if I stay engaged): my army deals 50 → primitive dies (0HP). Primitive deals 50 → my army at 0 → dies. Both die! Actually order/rounding matters. If both deal simultaneously, my army dies too. Bad.\n\nHmm, but does damage scale with HP? Not stated. Base damage 50 per army per round regardless of HP. So a 50HP army still deals 50.\n\nSo with 1 army vs 1 primitive: I lose the army in 2 rounds. Not useful.\n\nWith 2 armies vs 1 primitive: total attacker damage 100 → all to the primitive (only 1 enemy) → primitive dies in round 1 (100 damage vs 100HP). Defender's 50 split between 2 armies = 25 each. So both armies survive at 75HP. \n\nThen next turn, with 2 armies at 75HP, attack another primitive: they die again at 75→50? Each takes 25 → 50HP. Third attack: 25HP each. Fourth: dead. Hmm, so 2 armies can capture ~2-3 tiles before needing healing (heal +25/turn when not engaged and supplied).\n\nWith 3 armies vs 1 primitive: damage 150 → primitive dies; defender's 50 split 3 ways ≈ 17 each. So 3 armies take 17 damage per capture → can do 5 captures.\n\nEfficiency: more armies per attack = less damage. But recruiting is limited by 1/turn per barracks and equipment cost.\n\nAlso important: attacking a tile with 2 armies — both armies end up on the captured tile. Then they can attack the next adjacent tile.\n\nPlan: T5 recruit army#1. T6 buy 5 equipment (~41) + recruit #2 → attack with both at (29,23) or (29,25)... Wait, actually: can I recruit at T5 and T6 both at 碧庭 (1 per barracks per turn)? Yes.\n\nAlternatively: to save a turn, attack at T6 with 2 armies.\n\nHmm, but there's another consideration: 齐's location is unknown. Should I spy on 齐 (100金)? Treasury 263 - recruit materials (in stock) = 263. Spy 100 → 163. Then T6 buy equipment 41 → 122. That's very thin. But expansion income might come.\n\nActually, let's think about cash flow. Income in gold: zero. Expenses: equipment 40-45 per army, supplies if buying, wood if buying. My only gold source is selling goods. Let me estimate my production: food 5/turn, wood 4/turn (minus 1 fuel for 能源厂), ore 1/turn. If I sell all surplus: food 5*2 = 10, wood 3*2.7 = 8, ore 4 → ~22 gold/turn. But I need food for recruiting (10/army) and supplies.\n\nSo my gold income is ~20/turn max. That means each army costs ~2 turns of income. Expansion is the only way to get rich (gold deposits).\n\nAlternatively sell ore stock (13 * 3.4 = 44, but ore is cheap now; wait for 4+).\n\nLet me prioritize: recruit army#1 now. Sell a bit of food? I have 31 food; recruit takes 10 → 21. Farm income 5/turn. I'll need 10 more at T6. So keep food.\n\nActually, I could sell 10 food now at 2.1 = ~21 gold. Marginal. Better: sell 10 wood? Only 9. No.\n\nHmm, what about the 木头 price 2.7 (贵)? I could sell 5 wood for ~13. But I need wood for construction (each building 5, 兵营 20). Buy back later at 2.0 = fine actually. Selling high/buying low is good trade. But margins are tiny. Skip.\n\nDecision T5:\n1. recruit 1 步兵 at 碧庭.\n2. Maybe move it? It's at 碧庭 (own tile). No move needed.\n3. Consider: build 补给厂 (200金+12木)? Can't afford