181 + income ~20/turn (if I sell). Tight but workable.\n\nActually, maybe I should sell ore (13 units, price 3.4 贱 — below baseline 4). Better to wait for price to return to 4. Ore isn't needed much (only 补给厂/装备厂 use it). I'll sell ~10 ore when price ≥4.\n\nLet me now act: recruit 步兵×1 at 碧庭.\n\nThen end turn. Also maybe build something cheap with remaining wood? I have 9 wood; recruit doesn't use wood. Building a farm (60金+5木) at 苍堰 (耕2, has 1 farm) → +1 food/turn. Food is needed for recruits (10/turn each). My farm income is 5/turn, so 1 recruit/turn is sustainable. Skip building to save cash.\n\nHmm, but idle tiles = lost income. Cash is the constraint though. Let me do one cheap thing: 云谷 农场? 75金. No, save cash.\n\nDecision: recruit only. Then end turn.\n\nActually wait. Let me reconsider the attack timing more. If I recruit T5 and T6, attack T6 with 2 armies... but recruitment happens during my action phase, and the army exists immediately (can it move/attack the same turn?). Probably yes — recruited armies can act. At T6, army#2 is recruited, then both attack (29,23). Let me verify armies can act on recruitment turn — likely yes.\n\nSo T5: recruit #1. T6: buy equip, recruit #2, attack (29,23)P with both.\n\nOne more thing: should I attack (29,23)P or (30,25)P or (29,26)P? Which tile likely has gold? Unknown. Consider direction: expanding east/northeast (30,x) moves away from 秦 (northwest) — good, less collision risk. Also unknown where 齐 is.\n\n(29,23) is adjacent to 碧庭(29,24) — closest. Let's target that first; it's also adjacent to (30,23)P, (28,22)D, (29,22)M, (27,23)P etc.\n\nAlright. Also, the primitive tiles' terrain matters for their defense: P=0%, F=forest 10%, H=hills 25%, D=desert -10%, M=mountain 50%. So attack plains/deserts first. (29,23)P is good. Desert (27,25)D, (26,25)D, (28,22)D are -10% def (easier) but not adjacent to 碧庭... (28,22)D is adjacent to 宣邑/云谷.\n\nLet me act: recruit 1 步兵 at 碧庭.",
