            "reasoning_content": "Turn 7. I captured 望坡 (29,23) — plains, 耕地x2, no gold, no wood, no oil. My armies took minimal damage (99HP each — interesting, the primitive died before dealing damage? Or damage was reduced. Both at 99HP, so nearly no losses. Lucky — maybe the primitive dealt 50 split = 25 but... they show 99HP. Perhaps healing occurred? Or the primitive's damage was minimal. Anyway, great.)\n\nNow: 2 armies at 望坡 (29,23), both can act. Adjacent wasteland tiles from 望坡: (29,22)M, (28,22)D, (30,22)F, (27,23)P, (29,24)mine, (28,23)mine, (30,23)P, (28,22)D, (30,24)H, (29,22)M.\n\nOptions: attack (30,23)P or (27,23)P (plains, 0% def) with both armies → capture another tile.\n\nCash: 220. Equipment 0, price 8.8 (贵). Recruiting army#3 costs 10粮+5装 = need to buy 5 equipment (~45). Food 21.\n\nSupply: 7 in stock, 2 armies = 2/turn → 3 turns left. 补给厂 costs 200金+12木 — that would drain my treasury. Alternatively buy 补给 at 5/each.\n\nHmm. Let me think about the strategic picture:\n- My 6 tiles have no gold, no oil. Only 1 ore total. So my long-term income is limited: farms (耕地: 苍堰2, 宣邑2, 云谷3, 岚栅1, 望坡2, 碧庭5 = 15), lumber (苍堰1, 宣邑1, 云谷2, 岚栅2, 碧庭2 = 9), mine 1. Max production value ≈ 15*2 + 9*2 + 1*4 = 52 gold/turn if fully built out — but building all that costs ~15*60 + 9*55 + ... ≈ 1400 gold, which I don't have.\n\nSo I must find gold deposits. Wasteland tiles' resources are hidden until captured. 望坡 had none. Keep expanding to find gold/oil.\n\nAlternatively: is there a better economic play? Selling wood at 2.4 (贵) — I have 15 wood and produce 4/turn. Wood is needed for construction. \n\nLet me think about the real constraint: I need gold income. Options:\na) Find and build 黄金矿场 (needs a tile with 黄金>0).\nb) Build up production and sell goods (slow, needs capital).\nc) Sell my stockpiled ore (15 at 3.3 = ~50) — one-time.\n\nSo expansion is key. Each capture costs ~5 equipment (45 gold) + food + supply. Cheap-ish.\n\nAttack plan for T7: 2 armies attack (30,23)P (east, away from 秦) — capture. Then T8: those 2 armies attack (30,24)H (hills 25% def → my damage reduced? No: \"每军基础伤害50，受守方地形+城堡防御%修正\" — the defender's terrain bonus reduces damage dealt to it. So attacking hills: 100 damage × (1-0.25) = 75 → primitive survives at 25HP. Not a one-round kill. So prefer plains/desert targets.\n\nBetter: attack (30,25)P? Not adjacent to (30,23) yet. From 望坡, plains targets: (27,23)P, (30,23)P. Also desert (28,22)D (-10% def → easier: 100 damage × 1.1 = 110 → kills).\n\nLet me plan a chain: T7 attack (30,23)P. T8 attack (30,24)H or (30,25)P... (30,24) is hills. Hmm, from (30,23) adjacent: (30,24)H, (29,24)mine, (31,23)?, (31,24)?, (29,22)M, (30,22)F. Beyond my current vision.\n\nAlternatively T7 attack (27,23)P and continue west/southwest toward (26,23)P, (26,24)P, (27,22)P — a chain of plains. But west is toward 秦... 秦 is at x=17-21, far away. Not a problem.\n\nActually, direction matters for where 齐 is. Unknown. Let me expand in the direction with more plains. Visible wastelands: P at (26,23),(26,24),(27,22),(27,23),(27,26),(29,26),(30,23),(30,25); D at (26,25),(27,25),(28,22); F at (29,25),(30,22); H at (28,26),(30,24); M at (29,22).\n\nSouth/east has (30,25)P, (29,26)P, (27,26)P. West has (26,23),(26,24),(27,22),(27,23).\n\nPlan: T7 attack (30,23)P with both armies. T8 attack (30,25)? not adjacent. Hmm.\n\nActually maybe split: attack (30,23) with 2 armies is safest. Alternatively attack two different tiles with 1 army each = both die. No.\n\nSo: capture 1 tile per turn with 2 armies (they take ~25 damage each per battle... though last battle they took only 1HP! Maybe RNG: the primitive's damage roll was low, or terrain modifies. Actually the primitive dealt ~0? Both at 99. Nice.)\n\nHmm wait, maybe the primitive died in the first round before attacking, and the 1HP damage is from something else. Whatever.\n\nLet me also consider recruiting a 3rd army this turn to speed up (3 armies = faster, safer captures). Cash 220 - 45 (equip) = 175. Then T8: 3 armies attack → capture. Also supply: 3 armies = 3/turn, stock 7 → 2 turns. Need 补给厂 or buy supplies.\n\nTrade-off: I'd rather have a 补给厂 (200金+12木) for long-term supply, but that's all my cash. Let me instead keep 2-3 armies and buy supplies when needed (5 gold each = 15/turn for 3 armies — expensive).\n\nHmm. Actually, let me reconsider: maybe slow down army growth and build the 补给厂 first (200金+12木, needs 1电: grid is 产2/需1 → 兵营1 + 补给厂1 = 2 → exactly fits). 补给厂 produces 2 补给/turn from 1粮+1矿. My ore income is 1/turn and stock 15. So it can run 1/turn → 2 supply/turn, covering 2 armies indefinitely.\n\nThat's a good long-term play but costs 200 gold (all my cash) and delays recruiting.\n\nDecision: I'll recruit army #3 now (45 gold for equipment) AND attack (30,23) with 2 armies. Then next turn, if I have cash (sell ore for ~50), build 补给厂.\n\nWait, but food: 21 - 10 (recruit) = 11. Farm income 5/turn. OK.\n\nHmm, but actually — is a 3rd army useful? Yes: 3 armies attacking 1 primitive → damage 50/3 ≈ 17 each, and can then split into 2 attack groups later (2 armies + 1 army... no, 1 army can't take a tile alone). Better: with 3 armies, one group of 2 attacks while 1 heals. Effectively 1 capture/turn sustained.\n\nLet me think about how many armies I can sustain economically. Each army: 1 supply/turn (5 gold value) + 45 gold one-time. My income ~15-20 gold/turn from selling goods. So 3-4 armies is the sustainable max without gold mines.\n\nOK, T7 actions:\n1. buy 装备×5 (~45)\n2. recruit 步兵 at 碧庭 (army #3)\n3. attack (30,23) with armies #1,#2 (at 望坡)\n4. Sell some ore? Price 3.3 (贱). I have 15. Need 1/turn for 补给厂. Sell 8 → ~26 gold. Hmm, selling at 3.3 vs baseline 4 loses ~5 gold. But cash is critical. Let me sell 6 ore (~19) to fund the 补给厂 next turn.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: maybe sell wood at 2.4 (贵) instead — 5 wood = ~12 gold, and wood income is 4/turn. Wood is needed for 补给厂 (12木). I have 15 wood; recruit doesn't need wood. If I sell 5 wood now (12金) and need wood later at 2.0-2.2, that's a good trade. Marginal gains.\n\nLet me just do: buy equipment, recruit, attack, and sell 6 ore to build cash toward 补给厂.\n\nActually hold on. Let me reconsider whether to attack (30,23) or (28,22)D. Desert gives defenders -10% → my damage ×1.1 = 110 → kills easily, and desert's own value: 建设惩罚+40% (bad for building). Plains 望坡 gave 耕地2. A desert tile is less useful. (30,23)P plains is better for future building. Also (27,23)P is plains.\n\nWhich direction to prioritize? East (30,x) is away from 秦 (NW). Let me go east/southeast: (30,23) → then (30,24)H or (31,23)/(31,24) unknown.\n\nDecision: attack (30,23).\n\nLet me execute: buy equipment → recruit → attack → sell ore.\n\nOrder: buy first (need equipment for recruit). Sell ore can be parallel with buy? Both market ops; independent. But selling ore and buying equipment are different goods, so no interference. Let me do them in one block? The recruit depends on buy. So: block 1 = buy equip + sell ore; block 2 = recruit; block 3 = attack.\n\nActually attack and recruit are independent of each other (attack uses armies #1,#2). So block 2 = recruit + attack.",
