            "content": "第8回合：补给只剩4、3支军队日耗3，必须先建补给厂；卖木粮凑够钱立刻动工。\n\n",
            "reasoning_content": "Turn 8. Key facts:\n- Treasury 194, food 16, wood 18, ore 10, equip 0, supply 4 (critical!).\n- Armies #1,#2 engaged at (30,23) vs 野人26 at 25HP. They'll kill it this settlement (100 damage vs 25HP) → capture. They took damage: 80/81 HP (so primitive dealt ~20 each... wait they were at 99, now 80. So the primitive dealt ~19 each. OK.)\n- Army #3 at 碧庭, 100HP.\n- Grid 产2/需1.\n\nSupply crisis: 4 supplies, 3 armies consuming 3/turn → 1 turn left. Must build 补给厂 (200金+12木) — I have 194 gold! Short by 6. Or buy supplies at 5 each.\n\nOptions:\na) Sell something to reach 200+ and build 补给厂 this turn. Sell 5 wood at 2.3 (贵) = ~11 gold → 205. Then 补给厂 200金+12木 → 5 gold left, wood 18-5+... hmm. Let me compute: sell 5 wood → treasury 205, wood 13. Build 补给厂: -200金 -12木 → treasury 5, wood 1. That's dangerously low cash but 补给厂 solves supply sustainably (1粮+1矿→2补给/turn; my income food 5, ore 1 → yes 1/turn production uses my whole ore income).\n\nWait, but grid: 能源厂 2电 vs 兵营1 + 补给厂1 = 2 → exactly balanced. Good.\n\nRisk: treasury 5 means no diplomatic actions, no equipment purchases. But income at settlement: I'd sell surplus wood/food each turn to rebuild cash.\n\nHmm, but is 补给厂 the best use of the last 200 gold? Alternative: buy 补给 directly: 3 armies need 3/turn = 15 gold/turn at market. 补给厂 produces 2/turn from 1粮+1矿 (whose market value is 2+3.2=5.2, but I produce them myself). So 补给厂 saves ~10 gold/turn vs buying. Payback on 200 gold = 20 turns. Hmm, that's long, but it's the only way to sustain an army cheaply, and my cash income is limited (~20/turn from selling goods).\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider: do I even need to keep 3 armies? If I have 2 armies, supply need = 2/turn. Still 10 gold/turn.\n\nAlternatively, disband? No disband command. Armies consume supply forever. If supply runs out, armies lose 10HP/turn and could starve to death. Hmm, that's actually a way to \"disband\" but wasteful.\n\nLet me think about the bigger picture: my economy is weak (no gold income). Total production value ≈ food 5 (10g) + wood 4 (9g) + ore 1 (3g) = ~22 gold/turn gross. Army upkeep in market terms: 3 supply = 15 gold/turn (if buying) — that alone eats almost all income! So with 补给厂, supply is covered (2/turn from 1粮+1矿 which costs me ~5 gold of foregone sales).\n\nSo 补给厂 is essential to keep armies. Build it.\n\nBut careful: 补给厂 needs 1 ore + 1 food per turn. My ore income is exactly 1/turn (1 mine) and stock 10. Food income 5/turn. So it runs sustainably as long as ore stock ≥ 0. Good.\n\nAnd it produces 2 补给/turn vs consumption 3/turn → deficit of 1/turn! With 3 armies. Hmm. So I'd still drain. Unless I build a 2nd 补给厂 (needs more power) or buy supplies occasionally.\n\nAlternatively, keep army count at 2 (supply 2/turn = production 2/turn → balanced). But I have 3 armies now.\n\nHmm. Let me reconsider. Maybe better: build 补给厂 (2 supply/turn), and accept a small deficit, buying 补给 occasionally (5 each).\n\nAlso: should I recruit a 4th army? No — can't afford equipment (8.9 each) and supply deficit grows.\n\nNow, expansion: with 2 armies at (30,23) about to capture, and army #3 at 碧庭. After capture, armies #1,#2 (80HP) at (30,23). Next target from there: (30,24)H (hills, 25% def — bad), (30,22)F (forest 10%), (29,22)M (mountain 50% — bad). Hmm, eastward is hills/forest. Alternatively move to (30,25)P? Not adjacent to (30,23): (30,24) is between → not adjacent (distance 2). Adjacent to (30,23): (29,22),(29,23)=mine,(29,24)=mine,(30,22)F,(30,24)H,(31,22),(31,23),(31,24) unknown, (28,22)? no that's distance 2 in x.\n\nSo from (30,23) the options are (30,22)F or (30,24)H or unknown tiles at x=31. Since x=31 tiles are not in my visible list... my vision covers adjacent ring of owned tiles. After capturing (30,23), tiles at x=31 should become visible. The list shows 可拓荒地 16 blocks — same as before, so x=31 not revealed yet (I own (30,23)? Not yet — it's still 交战/野外, capture happens at settlement).\n\nHmm, so the frontier eastward has hills/forest. Let me consider attacking (30,24)H with 3 armies: damage 150 × 0.75 = 112 → kills 100HP primitive in one round; defender deals 50 split 3 ways ≈ 17 each. That works! With 3 armies I can take hills too.\n\nBut army #3 is at 碧庭 (29,24) — is (30,24) adjacent to 碧庭? Yes: (29,24)→(30,24) is 1 tile. So army #3 could attack (30,24) this turn... but alone: 50 damage × 0.75 = 37.5 → primitive at 62, my army takes 50 → 50HP. Bad.\n\nBetter plan: move army #3 to (30,23) [adjacent to 碧庭? (29,24)→(30,23) is diagonal distance 1 in both x and y → within 3x3 range of infantry. Yes, adjacent]. Then next turn 3 armies attack (30,24)H together.\n\nBut wait: armies #1,#2 are engaged at (30,23) this turn; they can't move (in combat). At settlement they win and capture. So next turn (T9) all 3 could attack (30,24) if #3 moves to (30,23) now.\n\nAlternatively, #3 moves to (30,23) this turn (mv into a wasteland tile that is a battlefield? Hmm — (30,23) is an active battle zone. Moving into a battle where I'm already engaged... risky/ambiguous. Let me instead move #3 to (29,23)望坡 (own territory, adjacent to both 碧庭 and (30,23)). Then T9: #3 moves to (30,23) and joins attack? That wastes a turn.\n\nActually simpler: leave #3 at 碧庭 (100HP, healing not needed). T9: #1,#2 (now at (30,23), ~80HP) + #3 attacks (30,24)H? #3 needs to be adjacent to (30,24): 碧庭 (29,24) is adjacent. So T9: all 3 attack (30,24) → damage 150×0.75=112 → kill. Good, no movement needed.\n\nHmm, but do I want hills? (30,24)H — hills have 建设惩罚+25%. Its value depends on resources. Alternatively attack (30,22)F (forest, 10% def): 150×0.9=135 → kill.\n\nLet me think about where the gold is. Unknown. Random. Just grab tiles cheaply; plains preferred.\n\nActually, another idea: instead of pushing east into rough terrain, push south/west where plains exist: (27,23)P, (26,23)P, (26,24)P, (27,22)P, (27,26)P, (29,26)P, (30,25)P. The (30,25)P is reachable via (30,24)H or (29,25)F.\n\nChain: (30,23)→(30,24)H→(30,25)P→(29,26)P... or (29,25)F→(29,26)P.\n\nOK, T8 actions:\n1. Sell 5 wood (~11金) to afford 补给厂. Actually let me check: 194 + 11 = 205 ≥ 200. Wood after: 13 - 12 (build) = 1. Then settlement +4 wood -1 fuel = +3 → 4. Tight but OK. Hmm, risky: next turn I might want to build something (farm 5木).\n\nAlternative: sell 8 wood (18金) → 212, wood 10 → build 补给厂 (-12木) → -2. Not possible. So sell 5 wood max, or sell wood + food.\n\nLet me sell 5 wood (11) and 4 food (7) → 212金, wood 13, food 12. Build 补给厂: -200, -12木 → 12金, 1木. Yikes, 12 gold left.\n\nHmm. Do I really need the 补给厂 NOW? Supply stock 4, consumption 3/turn → runs out at end of T9 (4-3=1 after T8 settlement, then T9 → -2 → armies starve). So I have until T9 to build it. If I build at T9, armies eat at T10 settlement.\n\nSo I could wait one turn, sell more stuff (income: +5 food, +4 wood, +1 ore at T8 settlement), and build 补给厂 at T9 with more cash left over. That's safer. But then at T9 settlement, supply = 4 - 3 (T8) = 1, then +2 (from 补给厂 active at T9? built T9 → active T10). Hmm: buildings built at T9 become active at T10 settlement. So supply at T9 settlement = 1 - 3 = -2 → starvation.\n\nLet me recount: supply stock 4 now (T8 start). T8 settlement: -3 → 1. T9 settlement: 1-3 = -2 → 2 armies go without supply → -10HP each. T10 settlement: 补给厂 produces +2 → 0-... it's a mess.\n\nSo build 补给厂 at T8 (this turn) if possible: it becomes active at T9 settlement → +2 supply, consumption 3 → net -1/turn. Stock: 4-3(T8)=1, +2-3(T9)=0, T10: -1 → deficit. Hmm, still deficit with 3 armies.\n\nSo either way I need to buy supplies occasionally or keep armies ≤2. OK.\n\nDecision: build 补给厂 this turn by selling 5 wood + a few food. Let me instead sell wood only: sell 5 wood → +11 (price 2.3→2.2?) → 205. Build: 200金+12木 → 5金, 1木. Then at settlement: +4 wood (lumber) -1 fuel (能源厂) = +3 → 4木; food +5 → 21; ore +1 → 11; supply: 补给厂 active? No — built this turn, active next settlement. So supply 4-3 = 1. Gold 5 + nothing.\n\nAt T9: I'd have ~4 wood, 21 food, 11 ore, 1 supply, 5 gold. Then sell wood/food to buy supplies (5 each) — with 1 supply and 3 armies, at T9 settlement they'd starve: supply 1 + 2 (from 补给厂) = 3 → exactly covers 3 armies → 0.\n\nSo T9: supply = 1 + 2 = 3, consumption 3 → OK, no starvation. T10: 0 + 2 = 2 vs 3 → deficit 1.\n\nSo I need either a 2nd 补给厂 (needs 2 more 电 → another 能源厂) or buy supplies. Fine — by then I may have captured a gold tile.\n\nAlternatively, don't build 补给厂 now; instead sell stuff and build at T9 while buying 2 supplies now (10金)? Let's compare: buying supplies costs 5 gold/army/turn forever (15/turn for 3 armies) — that's 100% of my income. 补给厂 is much better. Build it now.\n\nHmm, but wait: gold 5 is really dangerously low. Any market friction and I'm stuck. Let me sell a bit more to keep ~20 gold buffer: sell 8 wood + 4 food: 8 wood at 2.3 → ~18 (price drops to ~2.15), 4 food at 1.9 → ~7.5. Total ~25 → 219. Wood: 18-8 = 10 - 12 = -2. Not enough wood for the 补给厂!\n\nSo: wood constraint. I have 18 wood; 补给厂 needs 12. So I can sell at most 6 wood and still build. Sell 6 wood → +13 (price 2.3→2.2) → 207; wood 12 → build → 0 wood. Then settlement +4 lumber -1 fuel = 3 wood. Gold 7.\n\nOr sell 4 food (+7) as well → 214, gold 14 after build.\n\nLet me do: sell 6 wood + 5 food → ~13 + 9.5 = 22.5 → treasury ~216 → build 补给厂 → 16 gold, 0 wood. Food 16-5 = 11 + 5 income = 16.\n\nHmm, food 11 is below the 10 needed for a recruit — but I'm not recruiting (no equipment, no cash).\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider the whole thing: is it better to sell the 3 armies' worth of upkeep problem by NOT building 补给厂 and instead shrinking my military? I can't shrink. So build it.\n\nAlternatively, build 补给厂 but don't sell food — sell 6 wood (13) + 3 ore (9.6) → treasury 216.6. Ore: I need 1/turn for the 补给厂 input. Stock 10 + 1/turn. Selling 3 leaves 7, and consumption 1/turn while producing 2 supply. If I sell nothing, ore accumulates 0/turn (income