            "reasoning_content": "Very low cash (17). But at settlement I get +5 food, +4 wood (lumber) -1 fuel = +3 wood, +1 ore, and supply: 4 - 3 = 1 (补给厂 active next settlement).\n\nNext turn (T9) I can sell surplus: food 16, wood 3, ore 11. Sell wood at ~2.3 → 7 gold; food at 1.9 → ...\n\nIncome is thin. I need a gold source. Realistically: sell goods. Let me plan T9: sell 8 food (15), 2 ore (6) → ~23 + 17 = 40 gold. Then buy supplies if needed.\n\nHmm, this is a fragile position. The key question: will expansion pay off? Each captured tile adds 耕地/资源. But without gold deposits, I'm stuck at ~20 gold/turn gross income, of which army upkeep eats a lot.\n\nLet me reconsider: maybe I should stop expanding armies and consolidate. But I already have 3 armies (upkeep 3 supply/turn = covered 2/3 by 补给厂).\n\nAlternative income idea: 装备厂 needs oil (0) — no. 黄金矿场 needs a gold tile — none found yet.\n\nSo my only income is selling food/wood/ore. Total production: food 5/turn, wood 4/turn, ore 1/turn = 10+9+3 = ~22 gold/turn gross. 补给厂 consumes 1 food + 1 ore (worth ~5) and yields 2 supply (worth 10) → net +5 vs buying supplies.\n\nArmy upkeep: 3 supply/turn; production 2 → deficit 1/turn (5 gold).\nSo net: 22 - 5 (补给厂 inputs) - 3 (deficit supply bought) ≈ 14 gold/turn available for equipment/construction. Equipment 8.9 → one army's worth (5 = 45) every ~3 turns.\n\nThat's a slow but positive trajectory. Expansion adds tiles (each new plains tile with 耕地2 could give +4 gold/turn if I build a farm at 60 gold — payback 15-30 turns; and no gold deposits means building is a poor use of scarce cash).\n\nPriority: find a gold deposit tile. Keep grabbing free land (野人 tiles cost only battle damage) and check resources. Land itself is free income potential.\n\nSo T9: attack (30,24)H with 3 armies (150×0.75 = 112 → kill). Cost: ~17 damage each. Then check its resources.\n\nAlternatively attack (30,22)F (150×0.9=135, kill, take ~17 each). Which is more likely to be valuable? Unknown