            "content": "第9回合：补给厂已生效（正好自给3支军队），继续东进抢平原探资源，同时把第三军前调会合。\n\n",
            "reasoning_content": "Turn 9. Critical: supply stock 1, and 补给厂 built at T8 is now active (宣邑 shows 补给厂×1). But grid shows 产2/需1 — hmm, 需1? That means only 兵营 counts? Or 补给厂 not counted yet because it wasn't active during T8 settlement. It's active now (built last turn), so at T9 settlement: 需 = 兵营1 + 补给厂1 = 2, 产2 → OK.\n\nWait, but 电网 shows 产2/需1 正常 at the start of this turn. The 补给厂 shows as built. Hmm, maybe the 需 is computed from buildings active at last settlement. Anyway, next settlement should be 产2/需2.\n\nSupply: stock 1, production +2 (from 补给厂, needs 1粮+1矿) = 3 available; consumption 3 → exactly 0. \n\nNow cash: 17 gold. I need to sell goods to build up. Ore price 3.0 (贱, baseline 4) — bad time. Food 1.8 (贱). Wood 2.1 (贵 relative to baseline 2). I have only 3 wood.\n\nHmm. My income problem: everything I sell is at 贱 prices because I've been selling. Let me stop selling food/ore for a bit and accumulate? But I need cash for equipment (army recruitment) and construction.\n\nActually the critical strategic question: what do I want? Let me evaluate.\n\nCurrent state: 7 tiles, no gold deposits anywhere, 1 ore tile (凝里 has 矿石x1! Nice — that's a second mine possible). \n\nActually 凝里 (30,23): 矿石x1 耕地x1. So I can build a 2nd 矿场 there → +1 ore/turn → that ore feeds the 补给厂 (currently consuming my only mine's output).\n\nCash 17: a 矿场 costs 80金+5木. Can't afford.\n\nPriorities for T9:\n1. Attack (30,24)H with 3 armies? #1,#2 are at 凝里 (30,23) with 79/80HP; #3 at 碧庭. (30,24) is adjacent to both. 3 armies: 150×0.75 = 112.5 → kills the 100HP primitive in one round. Damage taken: 50 split 3 ways ≈ 17 each. Cost: no gold, just supply (already accounted).\n\nBut wait — is attacking worth it? Each new tile gives resources and vision. (30,24) is hills (建设惩罚+25%). Its resources unknown until captured. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively attack (31,23)P — not adjacent to my armies (from (30,23): (31,23) is adjacent! dx=1, dy=0 → yes adjacent). Plains! And (31,24)D, (31,22)F also adjacent to (30,23)? (31,22): dx=1, dy=1 → adjacent. Yes.\n\nSo from 凝里 (30,23), adjacent wastelands: (30,24)H, (31,23)P, (31,22)F, (30,22)F, (29,22)M, (29,23)=mine(望坡), (29,24)=mine(碧庭), (31,24)D.\n\nBest target: (31,23)P (plains, 0% def) → 150 damage kills easily, damage taken 17 each. And it pushes east away from 秦.\n\nLet me attack (31,23)P with armies #1,#2 (at 凝里) — 2 armies: 100 damage → kills 100HP exactly. Damage taken: 50 split 2 = 25 each → they'd be at ~54/55. Hmm, \"正好100\" might be a rounding risk. With 3 armies (including #3 from 碧庭 — is (31,23) adjacent to 碧庭(29,24)? dx=2 → no, out of infantry range).\n\nSo #3 can't join an attack on (31,23) this turn. Options:\n(a) #1,#2 attack (31,23)P (2 armies, 100 dmg vs 100HP → likely a kill, they take 25 each).\n(b) All 3 attack (30,24)H (adjacent to both 凝里 and 碧庭): 112 dmg → kill, take 17 each.\n(c) #3 attacks (29,25)F alone → bad (50×0.9=45, survives).\n\nHmm, (b) uses all 3 armies for one tile. (a) is faster (also 1 tile) but leaves #3 idle.\n\nActually, what about a bigger picture: should I keep expanding at all given no gold income? Each captured plains tile with 耕地 gives +2 gold/turn potential (farm), but building costs 60金+5木 which I can barely afford.\n\nHonestly, my bottleneck is cash. Let me think about how to get cash:\n- Sell production: ~20 gold/turn gross, minus 补给厂 inputs (1粮1矿 = 5 gold equivalent but they're consumed to save 10 gold of supplies).\n- Net: maybe 10-12 gold/turn. That's 1 equipment-buy (45) every 4 turns.\n\nAlternatively: reduce army count? Can't disband. But I could stop recruiting.\n\nHmm, what about 齐? Unknown location. If I capture (31,23) and beyond, I might reach 齐's territory. \n\nLet me think about a different income strategy: the market. Prices mean-revert to baseline. I've been selling wood at 2.3 (baseline 2) — that's fine. Ore at 3.0-3.3 (baseline 4) — I sold cheap. Bad. Let me hold ore (needed for 补给厂 anyway) and sell wood/food.\n\nActually, here's a thought: my 4 lumber camps produce 4 wood/turn; 1 能源厂 burns 1 → net 3 wood/turn = ~6 gold/turn. Farms: 5 food/turn; 补给厂 uses 1, recruits use 10 occasionally → net ~4 food = 7 gold. Mine: 1 ore/turn → consumed by 补给厂. So sustainable cash income ≈ 13 gold/turn. Plus selling stock (11 ore at 3 is bad).\n\nSo ~13 gold/turn. A 矿场 (80金) takes 6 turns of saving. A 黄金矿场 doesn't exist in my land. So I'm not getting rich. Growth must come from capturing tiles with gold/oil.\n\nTherefore: KEEP EXPANDING (cheap: only supply + battle damage) and hope to find gold/oil deposits. Each turn: 1 capture. That's the plan. And stop recruiting armies for now (3 armies is enough to take 1 tile/turn; equipment costs 45 = 3.5 turns of income).\n\nWait, but with 3 armies I take 1 tile/turn. With 4-5 armies I could take 2 tiles/turn (2 armies each + 1 spare). But supply deficit grows: 4 armies need 4/turn vs 2 produced → buy 2 supplies/turn (11 gold) — that would consume my entire income. Hmm.\n\nActually let me reconsider: build a 2nd 补给厂? Costs 200金+12木 and needs +1电 (requires another 能源厂 120金+15木). Total ~320金+27木 → 25 turns of income. And it produces 2 supply/turn from 1粮+1矿. Since my ore income is only 1/turn (1 mine), a 2nd 补给厂 would need 2 ore/turn → I'd need a 2nd 矿场 (80金+5木) at 凝里. Then: 2 补给厂 consume 2粮+2矿 → produce 4补给 → covers 4 armies. Grid: 兵营1 + 补给厂2 = 3电 → need 2 能源厂 (4电). Total investment: 矿场80 + 补给厂200 + 能源厂120 = 400金 + 32木 ≈ 30 turns of income. Ugh.\n\nSimpler: cap armies at 3 and accept buying ~1 supply/turn (5.4 gold).\n\nOK so the realistic plan: 3 armies, capture 1 tile/turn, prioritize finding gold/oil. If I find gold → build 黄金矿场 (+10/turn, changes everything).\n\nAlso: 18 wasteland tiles visible. If none has gold... I'd keep going further.\n\nHmm, another thought: should I consider attacking 齐 or 秦 for THEIR land (which has resources)? 秦's land: 沃坝 山地 with 矿场×2, forest tiles with lumber. Their spy report showed 国库457 and no gold mines either. So no.\n\nWhat about 齐 — unknown. If 