pply (army movement/attack) and yields a farm potential of 2 gold/turn if it has 耕地 (but building costs 60金+5木 = 30-turn payback at 2/turn... that's poor!). Hmm, farms pay back in 30 turns. Wood 2/turn: lumber camp 55金 → 27 turns.\n\nHonestly, my economy is weak. The only good ROI is gold deposits (22 turns) — and even that is meh.\n\nSo what's the winning move? Let me think differently.\n\nConsider: 装备厂 (矿1+油1→装备2) requires oil. 补给厂 (粮1+矿1→补给2) margin +4/turn at baseline. If I had more mines...\n\nWhat about 市政厅? Needs 6 buildings on one tile + 1电: 碧庭 has 4 (3 farms + barracks). Adding 2 more farms (60 each) → 6 slots → 市政厅 (500金+40木) gives 5 + 6 = 11 gold/turn. Payback ~45 turns + needs more power (another 能源厂). No.\n\nSo the fundamental issue: my income is ~13-20 gold/turn, and I have 3 armies eating ~15 gold/turn of value. Without gold deposits, I'm near break-even. Expansion into more tiles adds income potential but requires building cash.\n\nAlternative strategy: STOP expanding armies, minimize upkeep, and consolidate: sell accumulated goods slowly, build farms/lumber on captured plains tiles (each adds ~2 gold/turn), and grow the economy compoundingly. But that's a 30-40 turn payback horizon.\n\nHmm, what about diplomacy? If I could ally with 秦 or 齐, I'd get shared vision (see their land + adjacent ring) — cheap info. Alliance costs 10 gold (bloc_found → they must accept). An alliance also gives security. But bloc_found requires ALL invited members to accept; if they refuse, it miscarries. 10 gold is cheap. Do I want an alliance? It would drag me into their wars (defensive only for 共同防御). 共同防御 (proposed for 10 gold) = only defensive, and they must accept.\n\nValue: security while I consolidate + possibly shared vision (alliance shares vision; 共同防御 doesn't share map). Also intel: I could share_map with them for 10 gold each way... but that reveals my position.\n\nActually, given I'm not threatened (秦 is far NW, 齐 unknown), the main value of diplomacy would be 