            "content": "第11回合大好消息：新占的**凤垒(31,23)有黄金x1**（还有矿1耕2木1）——这是我唯一能改写国库曲线的资产，接下来全力攒钱建黄金矿场（200金+10木）。本回合先变现余货、补齐给养，三军合击东面平原。\n\n",
            "reasoning_content": "Excellent news! 凤垒 (31,23) is captured — and it has 黄金x1! Plus 矿石x1, 耕地x2, 木头x1. That's my first gold deposit!\n\n黄金矿场 costs 200金+10木 (plain). I have 21 gold and 6 wood. So I need ~180 more gold and 4 more wood. This is the priority — +10 gold/turn forever.\n\nHow to raise ~180 gold fast? Sell goods:\n- Food 19 (price 1.8 贱) → selling 15 = 27 gold. Bad price.\n- Ore 11 (3.1 贱) → 34 gold. Bad.\n- Wood 6 (2.0) → 12.\n\nTotal liquidation would give ~70 gold. Not enough. Hmm.\n\nAlternative: accumulate over turns (income ~13/turn) → 180 gold takes ~14 turns. Too slow! I want that gold mine ASAP.\n\nHmm, wait. Let me reconsider. Are there other options? \n\nActually — important: 黄金矿场 上限 = 本地黄金量 = 1. So 凤垒 can host exactly 1 gold mine (+10金/回合). That's the single best investment available. Payback 20 turns; it also compounds my ability to build everything else. Getting it ASAP is critical.\n\nFunding options:\n1. Sell all surplus food/wood/ore now: food 19 → keep ~5 for 补给厂+recruits; sell 14 = ~24 gold. Ore: 补给厂 needs 1/turn; my ore income is now 2/turn (宣邑 mine + 凝里? no — 凝里 has 矿x1 but no mine built; 凤垒 also 矿x1). Ore stock 11; 补给厂 uses 1/turn, income 1/turn → stock flat. So I could sell 8 ore now (~24 gold) and rely on... wait no, if I sell 8, stock 3, and income 1 = consumption 1 → stock stays at 3 → the 补给厂 keeps running. OK, so selling 8 ore is safe-ish. At price 3.1 (贱) that's 24 gold — losing ~7 vs baseline. But time value of the gold mine is high: each turn with the mine = +10 gold. So paying 7 gold in bad prices to get the mine 5 turns earlier is worth it.\n\n2. Also: capture more tiles? 凤垒 is captured. Next: (32,24)P, (32,22)P are plains; (31,24)D desert; (32,23)H hills.\n\n3. Sell equipment? None.\n\nTotal from selling: 14 food (24) + 8 ore (24) + 4 wood (8) = ~56 → treasury ~77. Still short of 200. Hmm.\n\nI also have 6 wood — need 10 for the mine. Wood income 4/turn (minus 1 fuel) → net 3/turn.\n\nSo realistically the gold mine is ~2-4 turns away if I hoard cash. Let me think about the fastest path:\n\nTurn 11: sell surplus aggressively → get to ~75-80.\nTurn 12: income +13 + sales → ~95.\nTurn 13: ~110.\n...\nTurn 16-17: 200.\n\nThat's slow. Alternative: reduce army upkeep / sell more? My total assets: food 19, wood 6, ore 11 = ~70 gold of liquid value. Plus ongoing ~13/turn.\n\nHmm, what about selling ALL ore (11 = 34) and letting the 补给厂 stop? Then armies starve of supply (-10HP each) unless I buy supplies at 5.4 (16/turn for 3 armies). Bad.\n\nWhat about this: my 3 armies are eating me. Should I reduce to 2 by letting one starve? That saves 1 supply/turn (5.4 gold) but wastes an army. Actually, hmm — the supply deficit of 1/turn is the core of my cash drain. With 2 armies: production 2 = consumption 2 → self-sufficient, no purchases. That saves 5.4/turn. But losing an army costs 45 gold of equipment + it slows capture.\n\nAlternatively: build a 2nd 矿场 at 凤垒 or 凝里 (80金+5木) → ore 2/turn → then a 2nd 补给厂 (200金+12木) + 2nd 能源厂 (120金+15木) = 400金 total. Too expensive; the gold mine is a much better use of 200.\n\nSo the priority is clear: get the 黄金矿场 at 凤垒 ASAP. Everything else is secondary.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider: can I get gold faster by other means? What about... no. There's no other income.\n\nHmm, but here's a thought: could I sell things at better prices by waiting a turn? Food 1.8 → will revert to 2.0 slowly. Not much difference.\n\nAnother consideration: 齐 and 秦 might also be expanding. If a rival captures 凤垒... no, I already own it ♥.\n\nOK so T11 actions:\n1. Sell food: keep ~6 for 补给厂 input + potential recruit. Actually I have 0 equipment and won't recruit (can't afford). So food is only needed for the 补给厂 (1/turn). Sell 14 food → ~24 gold. Food left 5 + income 5/turn = fine.\n2. Sell ore: keep 3 (buffer for 补给厂). Sell 8 ore → ~24 gold. Ore income 1/turn = consumption 1/turn.\n3. Sell wood: I have 6, need 10+ for the gold mine (10木) and future buildings. Wood income net 3/turn. Sell 2 wood (4 gold)? Or hold. Let me hold wood (I need 10 for the mine; currently 6 + 3/turn → 9 at T12, 12 at T13).\n4. Military: armies #1 (54HP), #2 (56HP) at 凤垒; #3 (100HP) at 凝里. They're hurt. Options:\n   - Attack (31,24)D (desert, -10% def → my damage ×1.1) with #1+#2: 110×(0.54+0.56 damage? no—damage is per army base 50 regardless of HP) → 2 armies = 100 base × 1.1 = 110 → likely kills the 100HP primitive. They take 50/2 = 25 each → ~30HP left. Risky but survivable. Then T12 with #3 joining we'd be strong.\n   - Or let them heal: they're not engaged now (battle won), so at settlement they heal +25 → 79/81 (if supplied). Healing is free and safe. Meanwhile #3 (100HP) could attack something alone? Alone, 50 damage → can't kill (100HP). Not useful.\n   \n   Hmm, what's better: 1 tile/turn or healing? My armies heal +25/turn when supplied and not engaged. If I attack with #1,#2 (54/56HP) now, they'd drop to ~30 and need 3 turns of healing. If they don't attack, they heal to 79/81 and next turn attack at full strength (taking 25 → 54/56 again, then heal). Steady state: 1 capture per 2 turns with 2 armies, or use all 3 armies to attack (but #3 is at 凝里, adjacent to (31,24)? (30,23)→(31,24) dx=1,dy=1 → adjacent! Yes! So all 3 armies can attack (31,24)D this turn: 150×1.1 = 165 → guaranteed kill, damage 50/3 ≈ 17 each → #1 37, #2 39, #3 83.\n\n   That's efficient: 1 tile/turn with all 3 converging. Desert (31,24) — resources unknown; maybe gold/oil!\n\n   Actually wait, is attacking a desert worth it? Desert has 建设惩罚+40%, so buildings there cost 1.4x. Still, resources (gold/oil) could be great. And it extends vision to x=32-33.\n\n   Alternatively attack (32,24)P (plains) — but not adjacent to my armies (from 凤垒(31,23): (32,24) dx=1,dy=1 → adjacent! Yes). Plains, 0% def: 150 damage → kill, take 17 each. Even better than desert (easier to build there later).\n\n   Hmm, which target? (32,24)P plains vs (31,24)D desert. Plains is better for building. But also (32,22)P plains is adjacent to 凤垒 (dx=1, dy=1). And (32,23)H hills.\n\n   Let me pick (32,24)P — plains, opens up southeast toward x=33, y=24-25 (where (30,25)P, (29,26)P etc. are).\n\n   Wait, but there's a subtlety: attacking with all 3 armies means they all stack on the target tile. Fine.\n\n   Actually, hold on: is it wiser to keep #1,#2 at 凤垒 healing and only send #3? No — 1 army can't kill.\n\n   Let me attack (32,24)P with all 3 armies: expected 150×1.0 = 150 vs 100HP → kill (with variance, damage rolls seem to vary ±25%: earlier 2 armies dealt 75 out of 100 → 0.75 factor. So 3 armies might deal ~112-150 → still kills 100HP). Good.\n\n   Damage taken: 50 split 3 → 17 each → #1 37, #2 39, #3 83. Then T12: #1,#2 heal to 62/64 (if supplied), #3 100. Hmm, supply is my constraint: 1 in stock + 2 produced = 3 = consumption 3 → exactly balanced. Good, no purchases needed this turn.\n\n   Wait, the panel says 补给仓1 and production +2/turn, consumption 3/turn → net -1/turn. So after T11 settlement: 1+2-3 = 0. Then T12: 0+2 = 2 vs 3 → 1 army under-supplied (-10HP). I'll need to buy 1 supply next turn (5.4). OK.\n\n5. Also: should I build anything this turn? Cash 21 + sales ~48 = ~69. Options:\n   - 农场@望坡 (60金+5木) → +1 food/turn = 1.8-2 gold/turn. Payback 30 turns. Not now — hoard for the gold mine.\n   - Nothing. Hoard.\n   \n   Hmm, but wait: 望坡/凝里/凤垒 are empty tiles (位0). Building farms there costs 60 each. My food income 5/turn; I sell ~14 food/turn... Actually food sales are my main income (5 food/turn = 9-10 gold). More farms = more income but 30-turn payback. The gold mine (20 turns) is better and also enables everything.\n\n   So: hoard cash → build 黄金矿场 at 凤垒 as soon as I have 200金+10木 (probably T13-T14).\n\n   Hmm, but actually, wait. Let me reconsider the price issue: 黄金矿场 200金. If I sell all my ore/food now at 贱 prices to get it 2 turns earlier, that's +20 gold of mine income vs ~10 gold lost in price. Worth it.\n\nLet me now also think: should I sell ALL 11 ore (34 gold) and stop the 补给厂? If the 补给厂 stops, armies lose supply → -10HP each. But I could then buy supplies at 5.4 (16/turn for 3 armies) — that's much worse than 1 ore/turn (3 gold). Keep 3-4 ore.\n\nPlan T11:\n1. sell 粮食 13 (keep 6) → ~22 gold\n2. sell 矿石 7 (keep 4) → ~21 gold\n3. attack (32,24) with [1,2,3]\n4. treasury → ~64. Wood 6 (→ 9 at settlement).\n\nThen T12: sell food 5 + wood 3 → +13 → ~77+13 = 90. Buy 1 supply (-5.4). Hmm, cash grows slowly. T13: ~105. T14: ~120... That's too slow for 200!\n\nUgh. Let me think harder. My income is only ~13-15 gold/turn because I have few productive buildings and prices are low. The gold mine costs 200. So ~10 turns of hoarding. That's terrible.\n\nAlternative: Can I get money faster? What about selling MORE assets: my total liquid assets are food 19, wood 6, ore 11 = ~70 gold. That's it. Everything else is buildings (illiquid).\n\nSo: 黄金矿场 at ~T15-16 if I hoard everything. Hmm.\n\nIs there any other way to get gold? \n- Diplomacy: gift? No. \n- 市政厅: costs 500, gives 11/turn — worse.\n- War: attacking 齐/秦 for their land? They have no gold either (秦 confirmed).\n- Stealing? No.\n\nHmm, what about capturing more resource-rich tiles and selling their output? E.g., 凤垒 has 耕2 矿1 木1 金1 — building a full set there (farm 60, mine 80, lumber 50) = 190 gold for 2+4+2 = 8 gold/turn income (payback 24 turns). Also 凝里 (矿1耕1).\n\nActually here's the thing: my income is limited by how much I can produce and sell. Currently: food 5/turn, wood 4/turn, ore 1/turn → gross ~21 gold/turn at current prices; minus 补给厂 inputs (1粮+1矿 = 5) → ~16 net; minus supply deficit (1 = 5.4) → ~10 net/turn. Ugh, 10/turn.\n\nTo reach 200: 20 turns of pure hoarding, or invest in production (which has ~25-30 turn payback but compounds).\n\nAlternatively — reduce army count to save supply! If I had 2 armies: consumption 2 = production 2 → no purchases → +5.4/turn saved. And I stop attacking (armies heal). Hmm, but 3 armies = 1 capture/turn which yields tiles with resources (like 凤垒's gold!). The gold at 凤垒 was a jackpot.\n\nLet me think about the value of the gold mine: +10/turn forever. If I get it at T16 instead of T12, I lose ~40 gold. So it's worth spending ~40 gold of \"bad price\" selling to accelerate.\n\nSo: liquidate more aggressively. Sell 15 food (26), 8 ore (24), 4 wood (8) = 58 → treasury 79. Wood 2, food 4, ore 3. Then T12: income food +5, wood +4-1 = +3, ore +1; 补给厂 needs 1粮+1矿 → food 8, ore 3 → sell surplus: 8 food (14), 3 wood (6) → treasury ~100. T13: similar → ~120. T14: ~140... still slow.\n\nHmm. The math is grim: ~20 gold/turn max income. \n\nWait wait. Let me reconsider. Maybe I'm wrong about something. Let me re-examine: is 黄金矿场 really the only gold income? Yes: 黄金矿场 +10金/回合, 市政厅 also gives gold. And selling goods gives gold — that IS income. So my \"gold income\" = value of production. Fine.\n\nSo the economy: I have 8 tiles. Full build-out potential: 耕地 total = 2+2+3+1+2+5+1+2 = 18 farms → 36 gold/turn gross. 木头 total = 1+1+2+2+0+2+0+1 = 9 lumber → 18 gold/turn. 矿 = 3 (宣邑1 凝里1 凤垒1) → 12 gold/turn. 金 = 1 → 10 gold/turn. Total potential ≈ 76 gold/turn gross, requiring ~18*60 + 9*55 + 3*80 + 200 = 1080+495+240+200 = ~2000 gold. I have 21. So I'm at ~1% of build-out. It'll take many turns of reinvesting.\n\nGiven that, the smart move is to reinvest ALL surplus into the highest-ROI buildings and expand to more tiles (free land with resources). ROI ranking (at baseline prices):\n- 黄金矿场: 200 → 10/turn = 5%/turn (payback 20)\n- 矿场: 80 → 4/turn = 5% (payback 20-22)\n- 装备厂 (needs oil): 240 → +6/turn = 2.5%\n- 补给厂: 200 → +4/turn = 2% (but saves supply purchases: real value higher since I buy at 5.4)\n- 农场: 60 → 2/turn = 3.3%\n- 林场: 50 → 2/turn = 4%\n\nHmm interesting: 林场 50金 → 2/turn = 4%/turn (payback 25). 农场 60 → 2/turn = 3.3%. 矿场 80 → 4/turn = 5%. 黄金矿场 200 → 10/turn = 5%.\n\nSo mines (gold and ore) are best. I have 2 more ore deposits available (凝里, 凤垒) → 80 gold each for 4/turn.\n\nBut prices: ore is at 3.1 (贱) → 3.1/turn = 3.9%/turn. Still good. And selling ore in bulk pushes the price down further... but prices mean-revert, and my sales are small relative to the market (market depth scales with countries; with 3 countries, my 8-unit sale moved price 3.3→3.1). Hmm, my sales DO move prices noticeably.\n\nNote: prices revert toward baseline each turn. So a steady 1-2 units/turn sale keeps prices near baseline. Dumping 8 at once crashes the price. So better to sell small amounts each turn: e.g., 2 ore/turn at ~3.5-4.\n\nOK. Revised approach: sell modest surpluses each turn (food 3-4, wood 2-3, ore 1), reinvest into the best-ROI buildings, and keep expanding with 3 armies to grab more resource tiles (expansion is nearly free: 17 HP damage per capture + supply).\n\nActually, hmm, expansion gives free tiles but I lack cash to build on them. Yet each new tile with 矿/金 is valuable. 凤垒 had gold! So expansion is like a lottery ticket that costs ~17HP and 1 supply. Definitely worth continuing.\n\nPriority: 黄金矿场 at 凤垒 (200金+10木) — hoard for it, and meanwhile keep expanding.\n\nLet me also reconsider: should I stop attacking to save supply/damage? No — expansion is the main growth engine, and it also reveals whether more gold/oil exists nearby. But my armies are at 54/56/100 HP. Attacking (32,24)P with 3 armies: they'd take ~17 each → 37/39/83. Then T12 they'd need healing (they heal +25 if supplied). So maybe attack every other turn: T11 attack, T12 heal (also #1,#2 at 37/39 → 62/64), T13 attack...\n\nAlternatively: T11 attack (32,24) with all 3. T12: heal. T13: attack (33,24) or wherever.\n\nHmm, but there's a subtlety: if I don't attack, do I still consume supply? Yes. So attacking \"for free\" while supplied is good value.\n\nLet me reconsider the damage math: does an army's damage scale with HP? The rules say base damage 50 per army; modifiers from terrain/castle. Earlier data point: 2 armies (99HP each) attacked 野人26 → it went 100→25 HP, i.e., 75 damage dealt (not 100). So there's a dice roll (0.75x). Another: my armies took ~19-20 damage each from a single primitive (which should deal 50 split 2 = 25 → they took 19-20, again ~0.8x). So rolls vary ~±25%.\n\nSo with 3 armies vs 100HP: expected 150 × ~0.75-1.0 = 112-150 → kills. Good.\n\nWith 2 armies at 54/56HP: 100 × 0.75-1.0 = 75-100 → might not kill. And they'd take 25 → ~30HP. Risky-ish but not fatal.\n\nDecision: attack (32,24)P with all 3 armies this turn (165 expected... no, plains: 150 × roll). Let me do it.\n\nWait — one more consideration on target choice: (32,24)P is plains (good for building, 0% def). (31,24)D is desert (-10% def → easier kill, but +40% build penalty). (32,22)P is plains too (adjacent to 凤垒). Let me take (32,24)P — it's on my south-east flank and plains; also from there I can reach (32,25), (31,25), (30,25)P...\n\nHmm, actually, let me think about which direction 齐 might be. If 齐 is east (x>32), pushing east collides. If 齐 is south... unknown. Whatever — I need tiles, and the collision risk is far off (they'd have to reach x=32 from their start).\n\nAlso: attacking (32,24) puts me adjacent to (32,23)H, (33,24)?, (32,25)? — new vision.\n\nOK, T11 action list:\n1. sell 粮食 10 → ~18 gold (price 1.8→1.7; keep 9 food)\n2. sell 矿石 5 → ~15 gold (keep 6 ore)\n3. attack (32,24) with [1,2,3]\n4. end turn (no plan revision needed until T19).\n\nTreasury after: 21 + 33 = 54. Wood 6 → 9 at settlement. Food 9+5 = 14. Ore 6+1-1(补给厂) = 6. Supply 1+2-3 = 0 → next turn buy 1-2 supplies.\n\nHmm, should I also buy supplies now (5.4) to avoid starvation next turn? Cash 54. Buy 2 supplies (11) → 43. But next turn I'll have income to buy. Let me buy 1 now as a buffer? Actually supply stock 1 now → settlement consumes 3 with +2 production → 0. No starvation this turn (1+2 = 3 = exactly enough). Next turn T12: 0+2 = 2 < 3 → 1 army underfed (-10HP). Since at T12 my armies will be at ~37/39/83, an extra -10 is annoying but survivable; better: buy 2 supplies at T12 when I have cash (~54+15 = 69).\n\nActually, let me just buy 2 supplies now (11金) to guarantee healing at T12 settlement — cheap insurance, and I'd buy them anyway. But prices: 5.4 now vs maybe 5.0 later. Buying 1/turn keeps the price up. Meh, let me buy 2 now (stock 3 → covers T11 and part of T12).\n\nHmm, but cash is the binding constraint for the gold mine. 11 gold = 0.55 turns of mine income. Fine, buy 2.\n\nActually no — let me not buy now; I'll buy at T12 after selling more. The risk is one army taking -10HP. Hmm, but healing (+25) requires \"补给够\" — if under-supplied, no healing AND -10HP. At T12 my wounded armies need healing badly. So buying 2 supplies now (stock 3 → 3+2 = 5 available vs 3 consumed at T11 → 2 left; T12: 2+2 = 4 vs 3 → 1 left) → all armies fed both turns. Yes, buy 2.\n\nLet me do: sell 10 food, sell 5 ore, buy 2 supply, attack (32,24).\n\nOrder: sells first (need cash), then buy, then attack. Sells are independent of each other (different goods). Buy depends on cash. Attack independent.\n\nLet me batch: sell food + sell ore + attack in one block; then buy.\n\nActually the buy needs cash from the sells, so do sells+attack first, then buy.",
