            "reasoning_content": "Turn 12. Key facts:\n- Treasury 48, food 9, wood 9, ore 6, supply 2, 3 armies all at 凤垒 (79/81/100 HP).\n- Market prices: food 1.2 (very cheap — crashed from my selling!), wood 2.0 (baseline), ore 2.8 (cheap), equipment 8.5, supply 5.6.\n\nImportant: food price crashed to 1.2 because I dumped 14 food. I should STOP selling food and let the price revert (mean reversion toward 2). Selling at 1.2 is terrible.\n\nWood at 2.0 = baseline; I need 10 wood for the gold mine and have 9 (+3/turn net).\n\nCash to reach 200: 48 now. Income sources: selling goods. At current prices: wood 2, ore 2.8. My surplus: wood 3/turn net, ore 0 net, food 4/turn (but price 1.2 → don't sell!).\n\nHmm, that's a problem: food is my main surplus product but the price crashed. I should hold food and sell wood instead. But food accumulates (9 + 5/turn - 1 for 补给厂 = +4/turn). Storage seems unlimited, so holding is fine — I can sell when the price recovers to ~2.\n\nAlso: with food piling up, maybe I should recruit an army (10粮 + 5装)? Equipment is 8.5 (贵) → 43 gold. Not now.\n\nCash plan: sell wood (3/turn × 2 = 6), and... that's only 6/turn. Plus I need to buy 1 supply/turn (-5.6). Net ~0! Ugh.\n\nHmm. That's bad. Let me reconsider.\n\nWait: what about ore? 6 stock, price 2.8 (贱 vs 4). Ore income 1/turn = 补给厂 consumption. Selling 3 ore = 8.4 gold.\n\nWhat else? I have food 9 + 5/turn. If I don't sell food, my cash income is tiny.\n\nAlternatively: use the food! Options:\n(a) Recruit armies (10 food each + 5 equipment = 43 gold for equipment). Not affordable.\n(b) 补给厂: consumes 1粮+1矿 → 2补给. Already running at max (1/turn).\n(c) Sell food at 1.2 = 6 gold/turn for 5 food. Bad but... hmm, actually is it that bad? Price will revert. If I hold 5 food/turn for 3 turns and sell at 1.8, I get 9 instead of 6 → +3 per batch. Small potatoes.\n\nThe real issue: my income is ~10-15 gold/turn max, and the gold mine needs 200. So ~15 turns. Meanwhile armies eat 3 supply/turn (16.8 gold at 5.6 if buying all... no, I produce 2, buy 1 = 5.6).\n\nHmm, wait. Let me reconsider the whole structure. Maybe I should reduce to 2 armies to eliminate the supply deficit. How? Let one starve: -10HP/turn → 100HP army dies in 10 turns. That's slow and it wastes an asset. But actually, do I need 3 armies? 3 armies = 1 guaranteed kill per turn. 2 armies = 100 damage × roll → often fails to kill in one round (2 rounds needed), so effectively slower expansion anyway. Keep 3.\n\nAlternatively: consider the value of attacking at all. Each captured tile: potential gold/oil/耕地. 凤垒's gold was the jackpot. Now I need 200 gold to monetize it. \n\nHmm, is there any way to get gold faster? Let me think about 齐/秦... \n\nWhat about this: my 8 tiles have 18 耕地 total potential. Food price is currently 1.2 because I dumped. If I stop selling food for 3-4 turns, the price reverts to ~2 and my stock is 20+ → sell 15 at 2 = 30. That's better than 18 now. OK.\n\nSo the plan is a slow grind. Let me think about optimizing the grind:\n1. Stop selling food (price crashed). Sell wood at 2.0 (baseline, and my wood net is only 3/turn; I need wood for construction).\n2. Actually, what generates the most cash per turn? Let me consider building a 2nd 矿场 at 凝里 or 凤垒 (80金+5木) → +1 ore/turn → sell at ~3-4 = 3-4/turn. Payback 20-27 turns. Can't afford (48).\n\n3. Hmm, what about the 黄金矿场 being the goal: 200金+10木. I have 48 + 9 wood.\n\nLet me think about a completely different angle: is it worth cutting military to save 5.6/turn and thus reach 200 in (200-48)/(10-5.6) ≈ 35 turns? No...\n\nBetter angle: increase income by building farms on empty tiles (望坡 耕2, 凝里 耕1, 凤垒 耕2) — but food price is 1.2 and farms cost 60. No.\n\nOK here's the thing: my income is structurally ~10-15/turn. The gold mine is the only big lever and it's 15 turns away. Let me consider: should I spy on 齐 (100金)? No — that delays the mine by 8 turns. Definitely not.\n\nLet me instead maximize: \n- Sell wood 3/turn at 2.0 = 6.\n- Sell food only when price ≥1.8.\n- Buy supplies only when price <5.5; stockpile when cheap.\n- Attack every turn with 3 armies (free, yields tiles).\n\nActually, hmm, wait. Let me reconsider: attacking yields tiles whose resources I can't build on due to cash. But what if a new tile has ANOTHER gold deposit? Then I could build 2 gold mines (needs 400金 total). Or oil → 装备厂.\n\nAlso, capturing tiles gives vision — maybe I see 齐.\n\nAlternatively, here's a thought: what about capturing the plains tile (32,24) with 3 armies now (they're at 79/81/100)? 150 × roll → kills. Take ~17 each. Yes, let's do that. Then next: (32,25)?, (33,24)?, (32,23)H, (31,24)D.\n\nActually, better target selection: (31,24)D desert vs (32,24)P plains. Plains better. Let me attack (32,24)P with all 3 armies.\n\nHmm, one consideration: should I split armies to grab 2 tiles per turn? E.g., 2 armies on (32,24)P (100 dmg, ~50% kill chance) and 1 on... no, 1 army can't take anything.\n\nLet me do the 3-army attack on (32,24).\n\nAlso: 补给 stock 2 + production 2 = 4 vs consumption 3 → 1 left. Fine, no purchase needed this turn.\n\nCash: 48. Should I build anything? A 农场 at 望坡 (60金+5木) — can't afford (48). Nothing.\n\nSell: wood 3 at 2.0 → +6 (price drops to ~1.9). Hmm, my wood sales push the price down too. The market depth with 3 countries is small, so my trades move prices. Let me sell 2 wood (4 gold) instead of 3.\n\nActually, let me think about the price impact: 木头 2.0 → selling 3 dropped it? Let me check T11: I sold 3 wood at 2.1→2.0. So 3 wood costs ~0.1 price. Small.\n\nLet me sell 4 wood (8 gold, price →1.9) and keep 5 wood (for immediate building needs; wood income 4/turn - 1 fuel = +3/turn).\n\nHmm, I need 10 wood for the gold mine. I have 9. If I sell 4 → 5, then +3/turn → 8, 11, 14... So by T14 I'd have 11+. Fine, and I can buy wood at 2 if needed.\n\nActually, the deeper question: should I keep wood or cash? Wood is needed for buildings; cash for the buildings. Wood at 2.0 baseline is