            "content": "第16回合：不再买高价补给（让2产/3耗的缺口在满血军队间轮转，省5.7金/回合），现金全部指向凤垒金矿；三军北上打平原(32,21)继续探资源。\n\n",
            "reasoning_content": "Turn 16. Status:\n- Treasury 94, food 12, wood 6, ore 3, supply 0, equipment 0.\n- 3 armies at 青牧 (33,22): 77/78/78 HP.\n- Prices: food 1.3, wood 1.8, ore 2.8 (all 贱), supply 5.7 (贵).\n- 12 tiles. No new gold/oil found. 秀里 has 耕5木4 (great for building later).\n- 29 wasteland tiles visible.\n\nNet income: selling 4 food + 3 wood at crashed prices = 5.2 + 5.4 = 10.6/turn gross; supply deficit 1/turn = -5.7 → net ~5/turn. That's really slow. At this rate, 200 gold is 21 turns away (T37).\n\nHmm. That's bad. Let me reconsider.\n\nKey realization: my problem is that I'm selling into a market I've crashed, and buying supplies at 贵 prices. The supply deficit (1/turn) is a huge tax (5.7/turn = over half my gross income).\n\nOptions to fix the supply problem:\n(a) Reduce armies to 2 → consumption 2 = production 2 → self-sufficient. Saves 5.7/turn. But losing an army (which cost 45 gold + 10 food) and slowing expansion.\n(b) Build a 2nd 补给厂 (200金+12木) + 2nd 能源厂 (120金+15木) + 2nd 矿场 (80金) = 400金. Way too expensive now.\n(c) Keep starving one army each turn (-10HP/turn). Over 10 turns that army dies. Actually... hmm, that's effectively option (a) but slower and it dies at random timing.\n\nHmm, interesting: what if I deliberately let #3 starve to death? It costs nothing (no gold) and reduces upkeep to 2/turn = self-sufficient. Then my savings rate goes from ~5/turn to ~10/turn — doubling income growth! And with 2 armies I can still capture tiles (100 damage × roll vs 100HP — often a 2-round fight, but 2 rounds = 1 tile per 2 turns... vs 3 armies = 1 tile/turn).\n\nBut wait: is a captured tile worth ~1 turn of an army's upkeep? Tiles are free land. With no cash to build on them, tiles are worth little. So yes, letting #3 die is economically rational!\n\nHmm, but the risk: armies are my only expansion engine, and if all 2 armies get worn down... Also, if 齐 appears and I need defense, 2 armies is weaker.\n\nHold on. Let me reconsider more carefully. Actually, is it really true that I can't sustain 3 armies? Let me recompute the true steady-state economics with prices at baseline (assuming I stop dumping and let them recover):\n\nProduction: food 5, wood 4, ore 1.\nConsumption (internal): 补给厂 1粮+1矿 → 2补给; 能源厂 1木 → 2电.\nSellable: food 4, wood 3, ore 0.\nAt baseline: 4×2 + 3×2 = 14 gold/turn.\nSupply need: 3/turn, produce 2 → buy 1 = 5 gold (at baseline).\nNet: 9 gold/turn.\n\nSo even at baseline prices, 3 armies cost 1/3 of my net income. With 2 armies: no purchase → 14/turn net. Big difference.\n\nSo: reduce to 2 armies → 14/turn → 200 gold in ~8 turns (from 94: (200-94)/14 = 7.6 turns → T24). vs 3 armies → T37. \n\nHmm, but wait: with 2 armies, expansion slows (2 armies vs 100HP primitive: 100×roll; the roll was 0.75 once and 1.0 once → so ~50% chance of a 1-round kill). Also each 2-round fight costs more HP.\n\nBut expansion isn't my income source — the gold mine at 凤垒 is. So prioritize the mine.\n\nDecision: let #3 starve. Actually hmm, that feels wasteful — #3 cost 10 food + 5 equipment (~50 gold). But it's a sunk cost. Its marginal upkeep is 5-5.7 gold/turn forever, and its marginal value is faster tile capture (worth little). So yes: stop feeding #3.\n\nBut careful: the engine might allocate the shortage to a different army each turn (e.g., #1 one turn, #2 the next), weakening all three. The T15 log says \"补给断粮（缺 1）：0 支军队饿毙\" — so 1 shortage, 0 deaths. HP went 100 → 77/78/78 for all three... wait, they were at 95/98/100 after T14, then attacked (33,22) → took combat damage ~17-20 each → 77/78/78. So the HP loss was combat damage, not starvation. Hmm, and did the starvation apply? \"缺1\" and 0 deaths. So one army took -10? Let me see: after T14 settlement they were 95/98/100 (per T15 panel). Then T15: attack (33,22) + supply shortage. Now 77/78/78. So they each took ~18-22 → that's combat damage (~17 split 3 ways + variance). Starvation -10 may or may not have been applied.\n\nHmm, if starvation is applied to one army, that army would be at ~68. All three are 77/78/78, so it seems starvation hit... unclear. Maybe the -10 was applied to all? No.\n\nWhatever. The plan: don't buy supplies; let the shortage ride. With 3 armies and 2 supply, one army is short each turn. If the engine picks the same army, it dies in ~7-8 turns (78HP → 0). If it rotates, all three decline slowly.\n\nActually, hmm, that's a bad outcome: all 3 armies weakening to ~50 and staying there (no healing since under-supplied). That's worse than deliberately losing one.\n\nAlternative cleaner approach: MOVE #3 far away from my economic core? No, upkeep is per army regardless of location.\n\nHmm, what about this: I could deliberately sacrifice #3 by attacking with it alone against a primitive (it would die in 2 rounds). E.g., #3 attacks (34,22)M alone: 50×0.5 = 25 damage to the mountain primitive; it deals 50 → #3 at 28, then next round dies. That's a clean \"disband\" costing one army. Then 2 armies remain, supply self-sufficient.\n\nBut wait — is 2 armies enough for expansion? 2 armies = 100 damage; primitive 100HP. With roll variance, often needs 2 rounds. In 2 rounds, my armies take ~50 total damage each round split → 25 each per round → 50 total → they'd be at 50HP after capture, then heal 25/turn for 2 turns. So effectively 1 tile per 2-3 turns. Slower but tiles are worthless to me right now anyway (no cash to build).\n\nHmm, hmm. Let me think about whether tiles are really worthless. Each captured tile adds potential buildings. But building costs 50-80 gold each with 25-30 turn payback. My cash is the constraint. So yes, more tiles ≠ more income until I have cash.\n\nBUT: there's a real option value — a tile with GOLD (like 凤垒) is worth 200金+10木 → +10/turn. Each captured tile is a ~10% lottery for gold. So expansion has option value. With 2 armies, exploration halves. Hmm.\n\nAlso: what if there are more gold tiles to the east/north? My 12 tiles yielded 1 gold (凤垒) — an 8% rate. Each new tile's expected value ≈ 0.08 × (value of a gold mine ≈ +10/turn for 30 more turns = 300 gold) ≈ 24 gold. That's substantial! So expansion IS valuable in expectation, IF I have the cash to build the mine when I find gold.\n\nBut I don't have cash to build a second mine (200). So finding gold now = frustration. Unless I hoard anyway.\n\nOK, let me simplify. The bottleneck is cash. Priorities:\n1. Get the 黄金矿场 at 凤垒 (200金+10木) ASAP. This is the single highest-ROI action available and it converts my one gold deposit into income.\n2. To do that, maximize net cash income: cut the supply bleed.\n\nSo: sacrifice #3 (or let it die), keep 2 armies, save 5.7/turn, and reach 200 by ~T24.\n\nHmm, but actually, wait. Let me reconsider: instead of killing #3, what if I keep 3 armies but they're all permanently under-supplied (-10HP/turn each in rotation)? If the shortage rotates, each army loses 10HP every 3 turns = -3.3/turn, while healing +25/turn when fed... Actually healing requires \"补给够\" — if the army was fed that turn, does it heal +25 even if another army was short? Probably the engine checks per-army supply. So 2 fed armies heal +25, 1 starves -10. Net: 2 armies at full HP, 1 cycling down. That's unstable.\n\nAlternatively: buy supplies only when the price drops below ~5.0 (it's 5.7 now). \n\nYou know what? Let me look at this from a different angle: what if I use the food I'm stockpiling more productively? I have 12 food and produce 5/turn; the 补给厂 uses 1/turn. Food sells at 1.3 (crashed). \n\nIdea: recruit a 4th army? No (upkeep!).\n\nIdea: build a 2nd 补给厂 to convert my food+ore surplus into supplies for 4 armies? Needs 2 ore/turn but I have 1 mine → would need a 2nd 矿场 (80) + 2nd 能源厂 (120) + 补给厂 (200) = 400. No.\n\nSo the decision stands: cut army upkeep. I'll let #3 die naturally by not buying supplies, and keep #1,#2 fed (they're the ones I use for attacks). Actually, if the engine starves a random army, my active attackers might get weakened. Hmm.\n\nCleanest: send #3 on a suicide attack against a nearby primitive, thereby removing it from the rolls. Cost: nothing (it's already doomed), and it might even capture a tile if lucky (unlikely alone).\n\nHmm, but that's also throwing away an army that could take a tile. Alternatively keep using #3 in attacks (3 armies = 1 kill/turn) while the shortage hits someone.\n\nHmm, let me think about the actual value: \n- Keeping 3 armies: -5.7/turn (buying supplies) OR armies degrade.\n- 2 armies: expansion at ~1 tile/2 turns; savings 5.7/turn.\n\nThe gold mine at 凤垒 is worth +10/turn. Getting it 13 turns earlier (T24 vs T37) = +130 gold. That dwarfs the value of ~13 extra tiles captured.\n\nSo: cut to 2 armies. How? Let #3 starve: it's at 78HP. With -10/turn it dies in 8 turns. But during those 8 turns, the shortage might hit #1/#2 instead.\n\nCleaner: attack with #3 alone at a desert tile (31,24)D [defender -10% → my 50×1.1 = 55 damage; primitive deals 50 → #3 at 28; next round #3 deals 55 → primitive at ~-? hmm 100-55 = 45, then it deals 50 → #3 at -22 → dead]. So #3 dies in 2 rounds while weakening the primitive. Actually the primitive might die too if rolls are good: round 1: 55 → 45HP; round 2: 55 → dead, but #3 takes 50×0.9=45 → 28-45 <0 → dead. Both die. Then the tile... \"守军全撤走/全灭时，进攻方自动占领\" — but the attacker is also dead. Hmm, ambiguous. Probably no capture.\n\nAlternative cleaner approach: keep 3 armies but move #3 to a distant tile? Upkeep is the same.\n\nHmm, what about: don't buy supplies and let the shortage fall where it may, while I keep attacking with all 3 (attacking armies don't heal anyway). The HP will settle around... each turn: 2 fed (heal +25 if not engaged), 1 starved (-10). If I attack with all 3, they take ~17 combat damage + 10 starvation on one. So they'd decline ~27/turn → dead in 3 turns. Bad.\n\nSo if I keep attacking every turn with 3 armies, I DO need to feed all 3.\n\nLet me reconsider: maybe the optimal is: attack every OTHER turn with 3 armies, and buy 1 supply only on the turns I attack? Hmm, the shortage is per turn regardless.\n\nLet me simplify with a cleaner strategy:\n- 2 armies is my sustainable force (self-supplied).\n- Therefore, remove #3. Fastest clean way: suicide attack. It costs 2 turns of #3's life and it might even help (weakening/capturing).\n\nActually, wait! Better idea: I can use #3 for ONE more useful thing — join an attack with #1,#2 to capture a tile THIS turn (3 armies = guaranteed kill), and start starving it afterward. Then over the next few turns, while #3 dies, use #1,#2 to attack every other turn (healing in between). Hmm, but the shortage during those turns would hit #1 or #2 randomly.\n\nAlternatively: #3 attacks alone and dies within 2 turns. During that time #1,#2 (fed, 2 supply = 2 armies) heal to 100. Then #3 is gone (or nearly), and I'm stable at 2 armies.\n\nLet me do that: send #3 alone to attack (32,23)H? Hills 25% def → my damage 37, it deals 50 → #3 (78) → 28 → then dies next round. Hmm, that just kills #3 slowly with no gain.\n\nOr send #3 to attack (31,24)D (desert, adjacent to 凤垒 but not to 青牧... #3 is at 青牧 (33,22)). Adjacent to (33,22): (34,21)F, (34,22)M, (34,23)H, (33,21)P, (32,21)P, (33,23)=mine, (32,23)H, (32,22)=mine.\n\n#3 alone attacking (33,21)P (plains): 50 damage → primitive 50HP, #3 → 50HP. Round 2: #3 deals 50 → primitive dead, #3 takes 50 → dead. Both die → tile probably not captured (attacker dead).\n\nHmm. So suicide is wasteful. \n\nAlternative: let #3 garrison and starve while #1,#2 attack. The shortage: 2 supply for 3 armies. If the engine feeds the ones... I can't control it. Risk: #1 or #2 gets starved occasionally (-10HP). But since they heal +25/turn when fed, occasional -10 is absorbable. Actually let's think: 2 fed + 1 starved each turn. If the starving rotates evenly, each army is fed 2/3 of turns: heal +25×(2/3) - 10×(1/3) = +16.7-3.3 = +13/turn net → all three stay healthy-ish! That's actually FINE — no need to buy supplies at all, and armies stay near full HP (capped at 100).\n\nOh nice. If the shortage rotates, nobody dies. If it always hits the same army, that one dies in 8 turns (and then I'm at 2 armies, also fine). Either way, NOT buying supplies is safe as long as armies are healthy and I don't over-extend. The risk is only if an army is at low HP and gets starved repeatedly → dies.\n\nSo: stop buying supplies entirely (save 5.7/turn), keep attacking with 3 armies every turn? No — attacking means no healing that turn, and combat damage ~17 + starvation ~10 → they'd decline. Let me attack every other turn: attack (take 17+10), rest (heal 25 for fed ones).\n\nActually, simplest robust approach: attack every turn with all 3 while HP > 60; when HP < 60, rest a turn (they'll heal since 2/3 fed). Monitor.\n\nLet me now also reconsider: with the saved 5.7/turn, my net income = ~10/turn (at recovered prices) → 200 gold by T26-27 (from 94: (200-94)/10 ≈ 11 turns). Plus I need 10 wood (have 6, +3/turn → fine).\n\nAlso: should I sell food at 1.3? It's crashed. My food stock is 12 and grows 4/turn net. If I hold, the price recovers. Let me hold food this turn and sell wood (3-4 at 1.8).\n\nHmm, but I need cash. Let me sell 4 wood (7 gold) and 0 food. Cash 94+7 = 101.\n\nActually, hmm, wood: I need 10 for the gold mine. Wood stock 6, income 4/turn, fuel 1 → net +3/turn. If I sell 4, stock 2 → next turn 5 → 8 → 11. Fine, and I can buy wood at 1.8 if needed.\n\nBut wait — is selling wood at 1.8 (贱) also bad? It's near baseline. My wood sales (4/turn) keep it at ~1.8. Alternatively hold wood and sell food later. Both are \"cheap\" goods now. Let me alternate: sell wood this turn, food in 2-3 turns when it recovers to ~1.7.\n\nAlso, I should consider: what about the 2 矿场 option? Ore at 2.8 is 30% below baseline. A 矿场 (80金+5木) → +1 ore/turn = 2.8-4/turn. Payback 20-28 turns. It would also let me run a 2nd 补给厂... no.\n\nGiven the gold mine is 5%/turn and reachable in ~11 turns, and everything else is ≤4%/turn, hoard. But hmm, 11 turns of pure hoarding with 3 armies at 100HP doing nothing much... Let me use them to grab tiles (free).\n\nActually, hold on. Let me reconsider ONE thing: the \"断粮\" warning at T15 said \"0 支军队饿毙\" — no deaths. Good.\n\nAlso, let me reconsider whether to attack again this turn. Armies at 77/78/78. If they attack (34,21)F or (33,21)P: 3 armies → kill, take ~17 → 60/61/61, minus starvation 10 on one → ~50. Then next turn they'd rest and heal.\n\nAlternatively rest this turn (heal to 100 for 2 of them) and attack next turn. Resting costs a turn of expansion but saves HP.\n\nHmm, expansion rate: 1 tile/2 turns with 3 armies (attack, rest, attack, rest) is sustainable. That's fine.\n\nLet me decide T16:\n1. Attack (33,21)P with all 3 armies? Or rest?\n   They're at 77-78. Attacking → ~50-60 after starvation. Then rest → heal to 75-85. It's sustainable but they'd hover at 60-85.\n   Let me attack: it's a plains tile (fast kill) and pushes north toward (32,20),(34,20) — new vision.\n   \n   Actually, which target? (33,21)P plains (north of 青牧) or (32,21)P plains (also north, adjacent to 新馆) or (32,23)H hills (adjacent to 凤垒/秀里/宝汀 — fills a gap in my territory!) or (34,21)F.\n   \n   (32,23)H is hills (25% def): 3 armies = 150×0.75 = 112 → kill. It fills the hole between my tiles (32,22),(32,24),(33,23),(31,23) — consolidating my eastern cluster, and hills give +25% defense for future. Its resources: unknown.\n   \n   Hmm, but the build penalty on hills is +25%. For a farm (60→75) it's meh. Still, filling the hole is nice for defense/cohesion.\n   \n   Alternatively push into new territory: (33,21)P or (32,21)P — plains, and reveals y=20 row (new).\n   \n   Since I'm fishing for gold/oil, new territory is more valuable (each new tile = a lottery draw). But so is (32,23)H (also a lottery draw, just rougher).\n   \n   Let me take (32,21)P: plains, adjacent to 新馆(32,22) and 青牧(33,22)? (33,22)→(32,21): dx=1,dy=1 → adjacent ✓. It reveals (31,20),(32,20),(33,20),(34,20),(31,21)M,(30,21)... new row y=20. \n\n2. Sell 4 wood (+7).\n3. Buy nothing (no supplies — let the shortage rotate; save 5.7).\n4. Build nothing.\n5. End turn.\n\nWait, one more: should I sell food to accelerate the gold mine? Selling 8 food at 1.3 = ~10 gold → gets the mine ~1 turn sooner. Value: mine +10/turn × (turns earlier)... The mine at T26 vs T27 = 10 gold. Selling 8 food now vs later at 1.7 = 13.6 vs 10.4 = +3.2 loss. Net: roughly break-even. Skip; hold food.\n\nHmm, but actually, I realize I should double check something: is it possible that prices are low because OTHER countries are also selling? The market is shared. 秦 had 4 lumber camps + 2 farms — they might be dumping wood too. Whatever.\n\nLet me act: sell 4 wood, attack (32,21) with 3 armies.\n\nActually, hmm, regarding the \"国策\" — I must revise by T19 (last revision T9, so every 10 turns → T19 deadline). I'll revise at T19.\n\nLet me go.",
