            "content": "第17回合重大发现：**东坊(32,21)也有黄金x1（还带耕地x4）**——我现在手握两座金矿点。全力攒第一座黄金矿场（200金+10木），清库存换金，三军顺手拿下相邻平原(33,21)。\n\n",
            "reasoning_content": "JACKPOT! 东坊 (32,21) has 黄金x1 AND 耕地x4! So I now have TWO gold deposits: 凤垒 (31,23) and 东坊 (32,21).\n\nEach 黄金矿场 = 200金+10木 → +10金/回合.\n\nCash 101. Armies at 54/56/56 HP (they took damage). Supply 0.\n\nNow the priority: build the first 黄金矿场 ASAP (200金+10木). I need 100 more gold.\n\nIncome: I need to sell. Prices are all 贱 (food 1.4, wood 1.8, ore 2.9). But time value of the gold mine is +10/turn, so accelerating is worth a lot. Let me liquidate: food 16 (at 1.4 → ~20, price drops to ~1.2), wood 5 (at 1.8 → 8), ore 3 (2.9 → 8).\n\nCareful: keep 1-2 food + 1-2 ore for the 补给厂, and keep some wood.\n\nLet me sell 12 food (~16), 3 wood (~5), 1 ore (~3) → ~24 → treasury ~125. Wood 2, food 4, ore 2.\n\nHmm, that's still 75 short of 200. At ~10/turn net (if I don't buy supplies), that's 7-8 more turns (T24-25).\n\nAlternatively, liquidate everything sellable: 12 food (16) + 3 wood (5) + 2 ore (6) = 27 → 128. Then T18: +5 food, +4 wood, +1 ore production; sell 4 food (5.6) + 3 wood (5.4) = 11 → 139... \n\nHmm. Let me think differently: is there a way to get 200 faster?\n\nWhat about selling MORE aggressively — i.e., dump all 16 food at once: 16 at 1.4 → price crashes to ~1.1 → revenue ~20. Then hold cash.\n\nWhat if I stop attacking (armies rest) to avoid damage? Doesn't matter for cash.\n\nOK, the reality: ~10/turn net. The gold mine arrives ~T26. Hmm, that's a long wait. \n\nAlternative idea: build the 黄金矿场 at 东坊 or 凤垒 — both cost 200. Can't split.\n\nHmm, what about a different angle: my income is capped by production. Could I increase production cheaply? The cheapest income boost: 林场 (50金+5木 → 2/turn). At 101 gold, I could build 2 林场 (100金+10木) — but wood is only 5. One 林场 (50金+5木) → +2/turn (at 1.8 = 1.8/turn... hmm, wood price 1.8).\n\nThat delays the gold mine by 5 turns (50 gold) but adds ~1.8-2/turn. Payback 25-28 turns. Given the gold mine is 5%/turn and lumber is 4%/turn, and the gold mine is the gate to everything... hoard.\n\nActually, hold on. Let me reconsider the whole \"sell at 贱\" issue more carefully, because it's costing me a lot. Food is at 1.4 vs baseline 2.0 — a 30% discount. My food production is 5/turn (4 sellable). If I hold food for 4 turns (stock 16→32) and the price recovers to ~1.9, then sell 32 food... but selling 32 units would crash the price to ~1.1 again, giving ~40 gold. Versus selling 4/turn at ~1.5 avg = 24 gold over 4 turns... hmm, wait: 4/turn × 4 turns = 16 units at avg 1.5 = 24. And 32 units at avg ~1.5 = 48. So per-unit revenue is roughly the same (~1.5). The crash from a big dump is offset by the recovery while holding. So there's no big arbitrage gain — the average realized price is what it is.\n\nOK so my income is fundamentally ~10-12/turn gross from production, and I should minimize spending (supplies!).\n\nLet me reconsider the supply question once more: 3 armies, 2 produced. Shortage 1/turn. Armies at 54-56HP. If the shortage hits the same army repeatedly: 56 → 46 → 36 → ... → dead in 6 turns. If it rotates, they hover.\n\nThe T15/T16 logs show \"缺1, 0支饿毙\" and all three armies have similar HP (54/56/56), which suggests the shortage rotates (or hits one and they all took similar combat damage). Actually let me check: after T14 they were 95/98/100. T15: attacked (33,22) → T15 panel showed 77/78/78 (T16 start). T16: attacked (32,21) → now 54/56/56. So each battle cost ~21-23 HP per army (combat ~17 + starvation ~10 = 27? close to 21-23 with roll variance). And they're all similar → the starvation rotates evenly. \n\nSo with 3 armies, 2 supply: each army gets fed 2/3 of turns. If they rest (no combat), net per army = +25×(2/3) - 10×(1/3) = +16.7 - 3.3 = +13.3/turn → they recover while resting. If they attack every turn, they lose ~17 combat + 3.3 starvation net ≈ 20/turn → dead in ~3 turns.\n\nSo: attack every other turn (attack, rest, attack, rest) → sustainable at ~50-80HP.\n\nNow, cash: 101 + 24 (liquidation) = 125. Need 200 + 10 wood.\n\nWood: I have 5, income 4/turn (minus 1 fuel). If I sell 3 wood now, stock 2 → +3/turn → 5, 8, 11 by T20. Need 10 at build time. OK.\n\nSo the gold mine is buildable around T23-25. Let me accelerate by selling aggressively now.\n\nHmm, actually — what about selling the ore (only 3, at 2.9)? The 补给厂 needs 1/turn; income 1/turn. Selling 2 ore leaves 1 + 1/turn income → the 补给厂 keeps running (flow-balanced). Risky if something disrupts. Let me sell 1 ore (3 gold) and keep 2.\n\nLet me also reconsider: should I attack this turn? Armies at 54/56/56. Attacking (33,21)P (plains, adjacent to 东坊 and 青牧): 150 damage → kill; they'd take ~17+3 = 20 → 34/36/36. Then rest next turn (recover to ~60). \n\nAlternatively rest this turn (recover to ~67) and attack next turn.\n\nValue of the tile: another lottery draw for gold (now 2/14 tiles had gold... hmm, actually 2 of my last 3 tiles? No: 东坊 was the 2nd gold tile found in 13 tiles). Each tile ≈ 8-10% gold chance. Expected value per tile ≈ 0.09 × 300 = 27 gold. But I can't build a 2nd mine (200 gold) for a long time. So marginal value of a 3rd gold deposit is low right now.\n\nHmm, but vision/land value... Let me rest the armies this turn to keep them healthy, and focus on cash. Actually no: attacking is free (no gold cost) and the HP cost is manageable. But if armies drop to 34 and then get hit... there's no enemy except primitives. Risk is low. But an army dying = losing 50 gold of investment.\n\nLet me think about what maximizes the gold mine timeline: nothing about attacking affects cash (except supply shortage which exists regardless). So attack = free option value. Keep attacking, but rest when HP < 40.\n\nCurrent HP 54-56 → attack this turn (→ ~35), then rest next turn (→ ~48+25... hmm, resting: fed 2/3 → +13/turn → after 2 rest turns ~61).\n\nAlternatively attack every other turn from now. Let me do: T17 attack (33,21)P, T18 rest, T19 attack, T20 rest...\n\nHmm, wait. Actually let me reconsider: is it better to attack (33,21)P (plains, north of 青牧, adjacent to 东坊) or (31,22)F / (32,23)H / (32,25)P / (30,25)P...? \n\nFrom 东坊 (32,21), adjacent wasteland: (31,20)M, (31,21)M, (31,22)F, (32,20)F, (33,20)M, (33,21)P.\nFrom 青牧 (33,22): (34,21)F, (34,22)M, (34,23)H, (33,21)P, (33,23)=mine, (32,21)=mine, (32,22)=mine, (32,23)H.\n\nBest plains target: (33,21)P. Let me take it.\n\nAlso (32,25)P is far (not adjacent).\n\nOK T17 actions:\n1. sell 粮食 12 (~16-17 gold)\n2. sell 木头 3 (~5)\n3. sell 矿石 1 (~3)\n4. attack (33,21) with [1,2,3]\n\nCash: 101 + 25 = ~126.\n\nHmm, should I buy supplies? No (save 5.8).\n\nShould I build anything? No — hoard for the mine.\n\nLet me execute. Sells first, then attack (independent, can batch).",
