            "content": "第20回合：休整一轮（三军59-62HP，不打仗、不买高价补给），继续小批量变现攒金矿钱——粮价1.2只卖6件、木卖2件，凑到130左右。\n\n",
            "reasoning_content": "Turn 20. Status:\n- Treasury 120, food 16, wood 6, ore 2, supply 0, equipment 0.\n- 3 armies at 启庐 (34,20): 59/61/62 HP. They healed (+25) — so they were fed? Supply stock 0 now, production +2/turn, consumption 3.\n- 15 tiles. New tile 启庐 (34,20): 耕3 木2 — no gold/oil.\n- Prices: food 1.2, wood 1.7, ore 2.9 — all 贱. Supply 5.8 贵.\n- Vision extended to x=35: (35,19)F, (35,20)P, (35,21)F — all wasteland with primitives. Still NO sign of 齐.\n\nPriorities:\n1. Gold mine: need 200金+10木. Have 120金, 6木. Need +80金 and +4木 (wood income +3/turn net → fine).\n   Cash: to get 80 more at ~5-8/turn... 10-16 turns. Hmm, slow.\n   \n   Wait — I have food 16 and ore 2 sitting idle. Food price 1.2. Selling 10 food = ~11 gold. The gold mine's value is +10/turn, so each turn earlier = +10 gold. Selling food at 1.2 gives me 1.2/unit vs a potential ~1.8 later. Selling 10 now = 12 vs 18 later, but accelerates the mine by ~1 turn (+10). Roughly break-even. Since I'm food-rich (16 stock, +4/turn), let me sell 6 food (~7 gold) and 2 wood (~3.4) → ~10 gold → treasury 130.\n   \n   Hmm, my plan says don't sell food below 1.5. But the time value of the gold mine is high. Let me sell a moderate 6 food.\n\n2. Military: 打一轮歇一轮 → T19 attacked, so T20 = rest. Armies at 59-62. Resting: 2 fed (+25 → 84-87), 1 starved (-10 → ~50). Fine.\n   Should I move them? They're at 启庐 (34,20), the far northeast corner of my realm, 12 tiles from my core. Remaining targets near them: (35,20)P plains, (35,19)F, (35,21)F, (34,19)H, (33,19)P, (32,20)F, (31,20)M, (31,21)M, (34,21)F, (34,22)M.\n   \n   Plains targets adjacent to 启庐: (35,20)P ✓, (33,19)P (dx=1, dy=1 → adjacent ✓).\n   \n   Attacking (35,20)P pushes vision to x=36 — where 齐 might be. That's valuable info.\n   \n   But per the rest cycle, attacking this turn means they'd take ~17 damage (59→42) plus starvation. Then rest 2 turns.\n   \n   Alternatively rest today, attack (35,20) tomorrow.\n   \n   Hmm, actually let me reconsider the whole expansion: is it worth continuing? Each tile is a lottery ticket for gold (2 gold found in 15 tiles ≈ 13%, plus 1 oil). But I can't build a mine without 200 gold. My tiles are accumulating (15 now, 8 of them empty of buildings). The empty tiles generate nothing.\n   \n   Actually, wait. I should reconsider: maybe I should stop expanding and start building farms on my rich tiles (秀里 耕5木4, 东坊 耕4, 启庐 耕3木2) to increase income. Each farm = 60金+5木 → +1 food/turn = 1.2-2 gold/turn. At the current food price of 1.2, that's a 50-turn payback. Terrible. At baseline 2.0 → 30 turns. Also terrible compared to the gold mine (20 turns).\n   \n   So the gold mine really is the priority. And more land doesn't help until I can build.\n   \n   Hmm, but here's a thought: what if I capture a tile that has GOLD and then... no, still need 200 gold per mine.\n\n   So: keep expanding only if free (it is free in gold), but the armies' HP is a limited resource requiring supplies. Actually, attacking costs nothing in gold. Let me continue at a slower tempo (attack every 2-3 turns) to keep armies healthy without buying supplies.\n\n3. Should I buy supplies? Stock 0, production 2, consumption 3 → shortage 1. Armies at 59-62 → they'll hover 50-90. No need. Skip.\n\nSo T20 actions:\n1. sell 粮食 6 (+7), sell 木头 2 (+3) → treasury ~130.\n2. Rest armies (no attack). Maybe move them somewhere useful? Moving is free. Where? If I plan to attack (35,20)P next turn, they're already adjacent. Fine, no move.\n3. End turn.\n\nHmm, that's a boring turn but consistent with the plan. Let me double-check whether there's a better use of 120 gold. \n\nOptions at 120 gold:\n- 矿场 (80金+5木) at 凝里/凤垒/宝汀 → +1 ore/turn = 2.9-4 gold/turn. Payback 20-28 turns. It delays the gold mine by ~8 turns (80 gold) but adds income. Earlier analysis said it's roughly a wash or slightly negative.\n- Nothing else affordable.\n\nLet me hold. Actually, hmm, let me reconsider: I've been assuming the gold mine takes ~10 more turns. Let me sanity check my income: gross production value at current prices: food 5×1.2 = 6, wood 4×1.7 = 6.8, ore 1×2.9 = 2.9 → 15.7/turn. Minus internal consumption (补给厂: 1粮+1矿 = 4.1; 能源厂: 1木 = 1.7) → ~10/turn sellable. Minus supply purchases (0 if I let them starve slightly) → ~10/turn.\n\nSo 80 more gold ≈ 8 turns → gold mine at ~T28. Hmm, and if prices recover to baseline, income would be ~14/turn → T26.\n\nAlternatively, if I build the 矿场 at T20 (80金), income becomes ~12.9/turn (ore 2.9 more) but I'd need to sell that extra ore each turn (pushing the price down). Then I'd reach 200 at: T20 cash 50, then +12/turn → 200 at T32. Worse than hoarding (T28). Confirmed: hoard.\n\nOK so T20: sell 6 food + 2 wood, rest armies, end turn.\n\nActually, let me reconsider one thing — is there any diplomatic play worth 20-100 gold? E.g., 共同防御 with 齐 if they're near? I don't know where they are. No.\n\nWhat about the possibility that 齐 is far away and I'll never meet? Then I'd have a peaceful game and just slowly build. Fine.\n\nLet me also think: is there value in a 城堡 anywhere? Defense only. Not needed.\n\nExecute: sell 6 food, sell 2 wood.\n\nHmm, wait. Let me reconsider selling food at 1.2. My food stock is 16 and grows 4/turn net. The price crashed to 1.0-1.2 from my dumping. If I hold and the price recovers to 1.8 in ~4 turns, my accumulated 32 food would sell for ~45 gold (crashing back). That's 11/turn over 4 turns — actually similar. Whatever, let me sell 6 now for the acceleration and keep 10.\n\nLet me do it.",
