            "reasoning_content": "Cash 130. Let me end the turn (armies rest).\n\nActually, should I move the armies? They're at 启庐 (34,20) — the far northeast. My core is at x=27-33. If I want to grab the western/southern plains ((32,25)P, (30,25)P, (29,26)P, (27,26)P, (27,23)P, (26,23)P, (26,24)P, (27,22)P), they'd need a long march (7-8 tiles = 7-8 turns of moving, and moving doesn't cost gold).\n\nHmm, is grabbing those tiles valuable? Lottery for gold/oil: 13% gold each. Expected value per tile ≈ 0.13 × 300 = ~40 gold. That's decent! But the march takes turns and each attack costs HP.\n\nAlternatively attack the nearby (35,20)P (adjacent) — same lottery value, no march. And it extends vision east (x=36) which might reveal 齐.\n\nLet me plan: T21 attack (35,20)P with 3 armies (they'll be at ~84/86/87 after resting). Then rest T22, then maybe attack (35,19)F or (34,19)H or (33,19)P.\n\nActually, from (35,20) after capture, adjacent: (36,19),(36,20),(36,21) — new territory. Good for vision.\n\nSo: end turn now; T21 attack (35,20).\n\nLet me end turn.",
