            "reasoning_content": "Treasury 143. Need 200 for the gold mine (and I have 10 wood — exactly enough).\n\nAt settlement: food 6+5-1 = 10, wood 10+4-1 = 13, ore 2+1-1 = 2, supply 0+2 = 2 vs 3 → shortage 1 → one army at ~13-17HP.\n\nLet me end the turn.\n\nActually, hmm, should I sell more? I have 6 food (need 1/turn for 补给厂, income 5/turn). Wood 10 (needed for the mine). Ore 2 (buffer).\n\nCash 143 → need 57 more. At ~10/turn → 6 turns → T28.\n\nCan I accelerate? Sell 4 wood (6.4)? Then I'd need to buy wood back (10 wood at 1.6-2.0 = 16-20). Net loss. Keep wood.\n\nSell food: I'll have 10 at T23. Selling 5/turn keeps the price ~1.1.\n\nHmm, let me think about whether to just accept the slow grind or make a different decision.\n\nAlternative: build the gold mine at 143? No, it costs 200.\n\nAlternative: What if I sell the wood stock (10 = 16 gold) to build the mine 2 turns earlier, then buy back wood at 2.0 (20 gold)? Net cost 4 gold for 2 turns earlier (+20 gold of mine income). Actually that's favorable! But wait, the mine needs 10木 at build time; if I sell wood, I need to have 10 wood when I build. Wood income is +4/turn (net +3 after fuel). So if I sell 6 wood now (9.6 gold), I'd have 4 + 3/turn → 10 wood in 2 turns, and cash 152.6 + 10/turn → 200 in ~5 turns (T27) with wood 13 by then. Hmm, roughly the same.\n\nSimplest: keep selling modest food surpluses and hoard. Let me end the turn.\n\nActually, one thing to consider: my armies are starving (shortage 1). One will drop to ~13-17HP. Should I let it die? Yes, per my analysis (2 armies = sustainable). But there's a subtlety: if the engine always starves the SAME army (e.g., the last one, #3), then #3 dies in ~2 turns. Then #1,#2 are fully fed and heal to 100. \n\nLet me end turn.",
