t (43 gold — need income).\n\nHmm, too tight. Alternatively skip building this turn, and next turn build both mine and 补给厂? No.\n\nActually, let me reconsider — maybe a better use of ~80 gold: 补给厂 is 200 (can't). Mine 80 → +3/turn. Farm 60 → +1.7/turn. Mine is best.\n\nLet me do: sell ore 5 (+15), sell food 8 (+13), sell wood 3 (+6) → treasury ~72. Build 珠苑 mine #3 (100, hills penalty)? Can't. 望邑 mine (80)? Can't (72).\n\nFine — accumulate this turn: sell and don't build. Treasury ~72, food 11, wood 8, ore 0, supply 5.\nTurn 11: income food+4, wood+2, ore+5 → sell ore 5+food 4 (~15+7=22) → ~94 → build 望邑 mine (80) → 14. Hmm, always broke.\n\nThe treadmill: I need a bigger cash injection. What assets can I liquidate? Nothing much — buildings are income.\n\nAlternative: slow down military, let economy compound? But armies already exist, upkeep 2/turn.\n\nHmm, actually let me reconsider the 装备厂/补给厂 route once more, since supply+equipment purchases are my two biggest cash drains (recruit = 43 equipment + supply 10.8/turn for 2 armies).\n\n补给厂 (200+12 wood): supply 2/turn from food1+ore1, 1 electricity (spare available). If I keep 2-4 armies, it saves ~10-20 gold/turn in supply purchases vs 4.8 of inputs → net +6-16/turn. Payback ~25-33 turns. Game length unknown; probably 50+ turns. Worth it once I have 200 gold.\n\nSo near-term goal: save 200 gold for 补给厂. Meanwhile mines.\n\nActually — maybe sell all food and buy back when recruiting? Food at 1.7 贱 is a bad sell. Ore at 3.1 vs baseline 4 — also 贱. Prices revert over time; maybe hold ore and sell when price recovers to 4? Holding costs nothing (no upkeep). Yes! Sell when price ≥ baseline. Buy equipment when ≤8.\n\nSo this turn: sell only surplus beyond a few turns of recruiting need. Keep food 19 (for 2 recruits), sell ore 5 (15) → treasury 63. Don't build (need 80). Hmm, but idle gold does nothing; a mine at +3/turn is 3.75% per turn return — build ASAP. Let me sell 4 wood (8) → 71, still short of 80. Sell 5 food (8) → 79... 1 short. \n\nOK: sell ore 5 (15) + wood 4 (8) + food 5 (8) = 31 → treasury 79, food 14, wood 7, ore 0. Short 1 gold. Don't sell anything else; next turn income +5 ore.\n\nAlternatively build 农场 at 望邑 (60) now: +1.7/turn, payback 35. Worse than mine but affordable → 79-60 = 19 left, wood 7-5=2. Wood 2 is risky (power plant burns 1/turn, wood income +2/turn → net 1/turn... fine).\n\nHmm, but wait — should the building be at 望邑 (mine, ore cap 2) or 悠澳 (farm, farmland 2)? 悠澳 farm = 60 → +1.7/turn. 望邑 mine = 80 → +3.1/turn. Mine better.\n\nDecision: this turn sell ore 5 + wood 4, keep food. Treasury ~71. Build nothing (or cheap farm at 悠澳 60 → 11 left). Then turn 11: sell ore 5 (~15) → 26+income... \n\nUgh, I keep going in circles. Let me simplify:\n\nTurn 10: sell ore 5 (+15) → 63. Build 望邑 农场 (60) → 3 gold. Hmm no.\n\nCleaner: Turn 10: sell ore 5, wood 4, food 4 → +15+8+7 = 30 → treasury 78, food 15, wood 7, ore 0. Then build nothing; turn 11: sell ore 5 (15) → 93 → build 望邑 mine (80) → 13. Turn 12: sell ore 5+food 4 → ~22 → recruit army 3 if equipment ≤8.3 (43 gold)... \n\nHonestly the difference between building a farm now vs mine next turn is small. Let me instead prioritize the 兵营 capacity: a 2nd barracks? No — 1 barracks recruiting 1/turn is enough pace; armies cost upkeep.\n\nRevised strategy focus (turns 10-20):\n- Grow mines to 6-7 (income ~20/turn) and build 补给厂 once 200 gold saved.\n- Recruit 1 army every ~2 turns when equipment cheap; grow to 4 armies.\n- Take 1 tile per 2 turns with 2-army stacks (rotate: stack A attacks, stack B rests/recovers).\n- Spy on 楚 when gold > 200.\n\nAlso — should I revise the plan now (required this turn). Yes, must call plan.\n\nTurn 10 actions:\n1. plan (revise 第2期)\n2. sell ore 5, sell wood 4 (wood price 2.0 贵? shows 现价2.0(基准2) 贵 — at baseline; fine to sell a little)\n3. build 望邑 矿场 if affordable after sells (78-80 short) → skip, build 悠澳 农场 (60)? It gives food 1/turn for recruiting — actually food is my recruiting bottleneck long-term (10/army at 1.7 buy = cheap; farms at 60 give 1.7/turn → payback 35 turns. Buying food at 1.7-2 is roughly as good as farms! Skip farms; buy food when needed.)\n\nMines: ore 3.1 vs payback 26 turns... also meh at current 贱 price, but ore price should revert to 4 → payback 20.\n\nHmm, what actually generates wealth here? Town halls: 500+40 wood → 5+1/building/turn. 望邑 with 5 buildings + town hall = 10/turn! That's much better ROI than mines (payback 50 turns though... 500/10). Hmm, but town hall income scales with tile buildings: 望邑 at 10 buildings → 15/turn.\n\nActually the real wealth: 黄金矿场 +10 gold/turn for 200+10 wood (payback 20-22)! But requires local gold resource — all my tiles show 黄金x0. New tiles might have gold! 悠澳 gold 0. Barbarian tiles' resources unknown until owned (or shown as ? in land panel). So expansion has a lottery element: gold-bearing tiles are jackpot.\n\nOK so expansion is valuable. Keep going.\n\nFinal turn 10 plan:\n1. plan revise.\n2. Sell ore 5 (+15) → 63.\n3. Build 珠苑 mine#3? 100 — can't. Build 望邑 mine (80) — can't at 63.\n   → Build 光崖 农场 (60)? Food not needed (buy cheap). \n   → Hold gold, don't build. 63 saved.\n4. End turn.\n\nHmm, holding cash is fine given supply needs. Actually let me sell a bit more food (19 held, need 10-20 for recruits; food price 1.7 is terrible — hold).\n\nLet me just: sell ore 5 (15) → 63; buy nothing; end turn. Then turn 11: +5 ore income; sell 10 ore → ~30 → 93 → build 望邑 mine (80) → 13.\n\nWait, actually, maybe better to build the mine at 珠苑 (100) vs 望邑 (80) — 望邑 cheaper. Yes 望邑 mine first.\n\nAlternatively, save for 补给厂 (200): turn 11-13 accumulate ~26/turn → by turn 13 ~140 → still short. \n\nI'll take the mine now-ish. Fine.\n\nLet me write plan revision and do sells.",
            "tool_calls": [
              {
                "id": "call_c5eed23b3fc640068c9e7c61",
                "type": "function",
                "function": {
                  "name": "plan",
                  "arguments": "{\"content\": \"【齐·国策 第2期（回合11-20）：以矿养军、稳步吞并荒地、攒钱上基础设施】\\n现状：6块地（新得悠澳9,26平原），2支步兵，国库紧张；收入≈粮+4/木+2/矿+5，卖矿为主，约20-25金/回合；秦远在东北(19,8)、第5回合情报显示其国库114、无军队，短期无威胁；楚位置未探明。\\n一、经济发展：\\n- 第一优先：把有矿的地块铺满矿场（望邑2、珠苑3、光崖3、永渚2、兴礁1），矿≈3-4金/回合，是唯一稳定现金流。\\n- 农场不再多建：粮市价1.7远低于农场回本线，征兵粮直接买（≤2.1时买）。\\n- 卖货纪律：矿石/粮食只在价格≥3.5/≥2.0时批量卖，低于基准就囤（囤货无成本）；装备/补给在≤8.2/≤5.0时才买。\\n- 中期目标（国库>250时）：光崖建补给厂（200金+12木，用掉电网剩余1电，产补给2/回合，省下外购补给的10金/回合）；再往后考虑兴礁石油厂+装备厂、望邑满6位上市政厅。\\n二、军事规划：\\n- 维持2支步兵一组打野（2军×50伤=100，一回合清100HP野人，己方各损25）；打完在原地歇1-2回合回血再战，避免单兵硬拼。\\n- 征兵节奏：装备≤8.2时买5装，每2-3回合补1支，目标第16回合前凑4支（两两成组，可同时开两条战线）。\\n- 拓荒顺序（由近及远、先平原森林后丘陵山地）：(9,27)F→(10,26)F→(10,27)P→(10,23)P→(11,24)P→(8,23)F→(10,25)F→(10,22)F；山地(11,25)/(8,25)/(7,23-24)留到最后。\\n- 补给仓始终≥军队数×3；断粮-10HP不可接受。\\n三、情报管理：\\n- 国库回200以上时派间谍刺探楚（100金），确认其位置/军力/扩张方向；在此之前不主动接触。\\n- 关注秦是否向南扩张（其可拓地含(20,9)丘陵、(21,7)森林等），若与我方扩张方向无交集则继续无视。\\n四、外交方向：\\n- 继续对秦、楚中立，不结盟不宣战；专心清野。\\n- 若楚与我接壤且抢地：先写信划界（约定各自方向），谈不拢再打；打之前确保有4支步兵且对方军力已探明。\\n- 若被宣战：优先求和止损（可小额赔款），绝不两线作战。\"}"
                }
              },
