            "reasoning_content": "Turn 13. State:\n- Treasury 12, food 19, wood 9, ore 5, equipment 0, supply 2.\n- 2 armies at 曜野 (9,27) with 70/71 HP, idle (可行动).\n- Grid: 产2/需1 (barracks 1). Wait, mine doesn't need electricity. So 需1 = barracks. Spare 1 electricity.\n- 7 tiles owned. New: 悠澳 (9,26) plains farmland2, 曜野 (9,27) forest wood3.\n- 20 barbarian tiles remain.\n\nCritical: supply warehouse 2, 2 armies consume 2/turn → after this turn, 0 → starvation next turn. Treasury only 12. Supply price 5.6 (贵). Need cash.\n\nSell ore 5 at 2.9 → ~14. Then buy supply 2-3 (~12-17).\n\nPrices are all 贱 right now (food 1.2! wood 1.9, ore 2.9). Food at 1.2 is terrible — don't sell food.\n\nOptions for cash: sell ore 5 (+14) → 26. Buy supply 3 (~17) → 9. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively: armies rest this turn (they're at 70/71 HP, healing +25 needs supply). If I don't buy supply, armies starve (-10 HP each). Bad but not fatal. Yet supply is a recurring cost of ~11 gold/turn for 2 armies — that's a big chunk of my ~25/turn gross income.\n\nHmm, let me reconsider: maybe I should reduce to 1 army? No — 2 armies = the combat unit. Actually...\n\nLet me think about the strategic picture more carefully. My economy: 6 mines now (珠苑2, 光崖2, 兴礁1, 望邑1 = 6 mines → ore +5? The panel says 矿石+5 last turn, and 望邑 mine is under construction → next turn +6). Farms: 望邑3 + 兴礁1 = 4 food/turn. Lumber: 永渚2 = 2 wood/turn. Power plant consumes 1 wood/turn.\n\nGross income if all sold at baseline: ore 6×4=24, food 4×2=8, wood 1×2=2 → 34/turn. Minus supply 2×5=10 → 24/turn net. But current prices are depressed (partly by my own dumping).\n\nThe problem: I keep dumping at 贱 prices because I need cash for supply. This is a trap. Better: hold resources when cheap, sell when prices recover. But then treasury stays near 0 and armies starve.\n\nAlternative structural fix: build 补给厂 (200 gold + 12 wood) to make supply self-sufficient — it converts food1+ore1 → supply2, using the spare 1 electricity. That eliminates the 10 gold/turn supply drain AND monetizes food/ore that I can't sell well. This is the key unlock. But I need 200 gold.\n\nSo the priority should be: accumulate 200 gold for 补给厂 as fast as possible. That means minimizing other spending and selling what I can.\n\nHmm, but wait: 补给厂 needs 1 food + 1 ore per turn to make 2 supply. My income: 4 food, 6 ore. 2 armies need 2 supply = 1 food + 1 ore consumed. Fine, leaves 3 food + 5 ore for sale (~12+20=32 at baseline).\n\nAlso for 4 armies (2 stacks), supply = 4/turn → need 2 补给厂 (or 1 厂 + buy).\n\nOK. Now, another consideration: should I keep attacking while broke? Each attack costs 25 HP/army and supply. Armies at 70/71 could attack (10,26)F or (10,27)P or (8,27)H next turn... Actually attacking this turn: 2 armies at 70/71 vs 100HP barbarian at (10,27)P (plains, adjacent to 曜野? (9,27)→(10,27) yes adjacent, dx=1,dy=0). Combat: my damage 100 → barbarian dies (plains no defense bonus). Barbarian deals 50 split 25 each → armies at 45/46. Take (10,27) plains tile. But supply: 2 in warehouse, consumption 2 → 0 left. Then turn 14 armies at 45HP unsupplied → -10 each → 35, and no healing.\n\nAlternatively rest this turn (heal to 95/96 if supplied), attack next turn.\n\nGiven supply=2 and treasury=12, the cleanest: sell ore 5 (+14) → 26; buy supply 2 (+~11) → 15; armies rest and heal to 95. Next turn: sell ore 6 (~17 at 2.9, or hold if price recovers) → buy supply, accumulate.\n\nHmm, but selling ore at 2.9 (baseline 4) is a 27% loss. Holding ore costs nothing... but I need cash for supply at 5.6 (also 贱-ish, 12% above baseline 5 — buying supply now is bad; better buy 4-5 when price drops below 5).\n\nWait — supply price is 5.6 贵 (baseline 5). Buying now is unfavorable but necessary to avoid starvation. Alternatively let armies go hungry for 1 turn (-10 HP each) and buy when cheaper. Armies are at 70/71 and idle; -10 → 60/61, no big deal, and they'd skip healing that turn. Actually starvation means no healing + -10 → net -35 HP. Then they'd need 2 turns to recover. Slows expansion by ~2 turns but saves ~11 gold... not worth it. Keep them fed; supply is the cost of doing business.\n\nActually, hmm: what if I disband... no, can't disband.\n\nLet me also consider: recruit army #3? Needs 10 food + 5 equipment (8.4 贵 = 42 gold). Can't afford now. Defer until 补给厂 exists and equipment ≤8.\n\nAnother idea: take a barbarian tile with a single army? 1 army (70HP) vs 100HP barbarian on plains: I deal 50 → barb 50; barb deals 50 → I'm at 20. Next round: I deal 50 → barb dies; barb deals 50 → I die. So no.\n\nWhat about attacking with both armies a hill/mountain? No.\n\nOK so the pace is: 1 tile per 2 turns with 2 armies, ~11 gold/turn supply upkeep. Income ~30 gross. So I can save ~10-15/turn → 补给厂 in ~15 turns. That's slow. Alternatively sell food stockpile (19 at 1.2 = terrible) — no.\n\nHmm, what about my wood? 9 wood, price 1.9. Need wood for 补给厂 (12). Keep.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the whole \"sell at 贱\" problem: prices are depressed globally (food 1.2 vs baseline 2, ore 2.9 vs 4, wood 1.9). Maybe 秦/楚 are dumping, or my own sales pushed them down. My policy of holding when cheap is right, but I need gold. The only real gold source is exports... plus 黄金矿场 (none available) and 市政厅 (needs 6 buildings on a tile + 500 gold).\n\nWait, one thing I haven't considered: 望邑 now has 5 slots used (3 farms, 1 mine, 1 barracks). At 6 buildings I can build 市政厅 (500+40 wood) → 5+6 = 11 gold/turn, growing with each building. That's the big gold engine for later. Needs 500 gold though.\n\nPriority order: 补给厂 (200) → then 市政厅 (500) on 望邑.\n\nFor now, turn 13 actions:\n1. Sell ore 5 → +~14 → 26.\n2. Buy supply 2 → -~11 → 15. (Warehouse 2+2=4, covers 2 turns.)\n3. Armies rest at 曜野 (no action) → heal to 95.\n4. Build something cheap? Can't afford (60+).\n\nHmm, could I build a lumber camp at 曜野 (50*1.15=57.5+5 wood)? Wood income +1/turn (sells at 1.9 → 1.9/turn, payback 30). Not now.\n\nActually, maybe better