            "content": "第19回合：先修订国策（已到10回合期限），然后按新判断行动——两军65/68HP，与其再歇一回合，不如直接南下打(11,29)平原（一回合可击杀、己方回到40左右），同时清仓筹钱。\n\n",
            "reasoning_content": "I'm on turn 19 with 71 gold and various resources, with armies positioned at 瑞台. I need to revise my plan before proceeding, and I'm considering whether to attack the plains at (11,29) next turn or rest my forces to reach full strength first.\n\nLooking at the economics: my income is roughly 6 gold per turn from selling ore, and attacking every other turn costs about 11 gold per turn in supply upkeep. The real constraint is that my current 2-electricity grid (from one wood plant) limits what I can power — a supply factory would consume my spare electricity, blocking future expansion unless I build another power plant. I'm weighing whether to build a second wood plant (120 gold + 15 wood) to expand my grid capacity to 4, which would let me run both the supply factory and barracks while leaving room for a town hall later.\n\nThe concrete priorities are: supply factory at 光崖 (200 gold + 12 wood) to cut upkeep, then the town hall at 望邑 (500 gold + 40 wood) for +11 gold per turn, followed by additional mines. The problem is that after building the supply factory, I'd only have 4 spare electricity — not enough for both the town hall and equipment factory, so I'd need that second wood plant anyway.\n\nBut there's a bigger question: should I keep expanding with my current armies instead of pouring everything into infrastructure? I've got 65-68 HP right now, and attacking (11,29) next turn could grab another tile. The expansion pace of one tile every two turns is sustainable, but I'm wondering if I'm over-investing in buildings when my armies are already paid for and could be seizing more territory.\n\nThe real constraint is cash flow. If I rest this turn and attack next turn, I heal to 90-93 HP, then drop to 65-68 after the attack, rest again to recover, and attack once more. That's one tile every two turns, costing about 11 gold per turn in supply upkeep. My gross income from ore is only around 17 gold per turn, so I'm barely breaking even on expansion while also trying to save for the 补给厂.\n\nBut here's the thing—once I build the 补给厂, it converts my own food and ore into supply, which means I can stop selling ore at the depressed price and let it recover. The factory produces 2 supply per turn from 1 food and 1 ore, which covers my 2-army consumption exactly. So the ore I would've sold gets converted into supply value instead, netting me about 8.5 gold per turn in value while also letting the market price stabilize.\n\nI'm also considering a second factory to support the 4-army push later, but that's getting ahead of myself. For now, I need to revise my plan since it's required next turn anyway, then decide on this turn's actions. I've got 71 gold and 6 ore—selling the ore would get me to 87, but I need 80 for the 望邑 mine, so I should sell and then build.\n\nActually, I'm reconsidering: the mine adds income but worsens the ore glut, whereas the supply factory is the real bottleneck. I could skip the mine, sell my ore and wood, and save toward the factory instead—that'd get me there in about 7-8 turns. I'm also eyeing the cheap food at 1.0 per unit; buying 20 food now for around 20-21 gold is a good hedge since I'll need it for the factory and can sell it later at 2.0.\n\nFor the immediate turn, I'm thinking: sell ore and wood to raise gold, keep just enough wood for the factory build, then attack the plains with my two armies since they'd survive the damage and gain a tile. I need to check if I can attack while also managing my supply situation.\n\nAfter the attack, I'll have 2 supply left, which covers next turn's consumption. The gold from selling ore and wood should get me to around 87, and I can decide next turn whether to build the mine at 望邑 or save for the factory instead. Let me go ahead and revise my plan, sell the resources, and execute the attack.",
            "tool_calls": [
              {
                "id": "call_78fa5884d6a24eea8da095ca",
                "type": "function",
                "function": {
                  "name": "plan",
                  "arguments": "{\"content\": \"【齐·国策 第3期（回合19-28）：先断掉补给出血口，再谈扩军】\\n现状：9块地（望邑珠苑光崖永渚悠澳曜野兴礁浩轩瑞台），2支步兵（约65/68HP），国库71。收入≈矿6/粮4/木2，全部低于基准价（矿2.8/粮1.0/木1.6），卖货被压价；两军每回合耗2补给≈11金，几乎吃掉全部现金收入——这是最大结构性问题。\\n秦：远在东北(18-21,6-10)，第5回合情报=国库114、无军队、5块地，短期无威胁。楚：位置军力全未知（间谍100金，等有钱再探）。\\n\\n一、经济发展（优先级从高到低）：\\n1) 【核心】补给厂（光崖，200金+12木，占电网剩余1电，吃粮1+矿1→补给2/回合）：建成即停止外购补给，并把卖不掉的矿粮转为自用，等于+8~11金/回合。攒够200金的第一时间建。\\n2) 补给厂建成后若仍要扩军到4支：再补1座木材能源厂（120金+15木，+2电，烧木1/回合），然后建第2座补给厂。\\n3) 矿场续铺（望邑第2座80、光崖第3座80、珠苑第3座100、永渚2座92×2）：在补给厂建成后再投，避免矿越多越砸价。\\n4) 望邑位满6后上市政厅（500金+40木，+11金/回合且不受市价影响）——中后期第一目标。\\n5) 不建农场（粮价1.0，农场永不回本）；征兵/补给厂用粮直接买（≤1.3时囤粮）。\\n6) 卖货纪律：矿≥3.4、粮≥1.9、木≥2.0 才批量卖；低于此只卖维持补给的最低量；补给≤5.0才买、装备≤8.0才买。\\n二、军事规划：\\n- 战术定式：2支步兵打平原野人=一回合击杀（100伤），己方各损25；打森林/丘陵需两回合、不划算。故**优先吃平原**：(11,29)P→(12,29)P→(10,23)P→(11,24)P，森林(10,26)(11,27)(9,28)留待3-4军时。\\n- 节奏：攻击回合后HP约40，休1回合（+25）再打，即2回合1格；不冒进、不让军队单独作战。\\n- 补给仓≥军队数×2；断粮-10HP不可接受。\\n- 征兵暂缓：等补给厂建成（军队维持成本降到0）后再扩到4支（2组），届时每2回合可吃2格。\\n三、情报管理：\\n- 国库>250时派间谍刺探楚（100金）——必须先知道楚的位置与扩张方向，否则侧翼随时可能挨打。\\n- 每5回合左右复核秦的动向（秦若开始征兵，说明它在走军事路线）。\\n- 收到任何来信先研判动机，不轻信。\\n四、外交方向：\\n- 对秦、楚一律中立；不结盟（盟约束缚大、且我无余力为他人开战）、不宣战。\\n- 若楚与我接壤并抢地：先写信提议各自扩张方向划界；谈不拢则避让其锋芒、转方向吃野人（野人地够多，不值当打生打死）。\\n- 若被宣战：立刻评估对方援军（共同防御/保障会传导），优先小额赔款求和，绝不两线。\"}"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
