            "content": "齐·步一军、齐·步二军 冲入 (11,29) 与野人交战，之后每回合结算一轮；可 retreat 撤出"
          },
          {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "【刷新】你齐 国库87 粮7 木11 矿0 油0 装0 补给仓4 | 军队2 | 收信0 | 关系:秦=中立  楚=中立 | 近讯见 events。继续你的行动，做完了调 end_turn。"
          },
          {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "",
            "reasoning_content": "Treasury 87. Armies engaged at (11,29) — will kill barbarian, take tile, drop to ~40/43.\n\nSupply 4 → after this turn 2.\n\nOptions with 87 gold:\n- Build 望邑 mine (80) → 7 left. But then no supply money next turn. Next turn income: 6 ore (+16), so turn 20: 7+16 = 23 → buy supply 3 (18) → 5. Tight but survivable. And the mine gives +1 ore/turn (2.7/turn) forever.\n- Or hold for 补给厂 (need 200): 87 + ~16/turn - 11/turn supply → turn 26ish.\n\nHmm, decision: mine now vs save for 补给厂. The mine adds to the ore glut but 望邑's 2nd mine is cheap (80) and also pushes 望邑 toward 6 slots (needed for 市政厅 later). Currently 望邑 位5/20.\n\nActually, 望邑 mine#2 → 位6 → unlocks 市政厅 construction there (when I have 500). That's strategically valuable.\n\nBut cash crunch: 87-80 = 7 gold, and armies need supply (~11/turn). Next turn: 6 ore income → sell ~16 → 23; buy supply 3 (18) → 5. Turn 21: 7 ore (with new mine) → sell ~19 → 24; buy supply... \n\nIt's workable but leaves zero buffer. Risk: if something unexpected (war, need equipment), I'm stuck. But nothing is expected — no threats nearby.\n\nAlternatively build the mine next turn (after selling more). The difference is 1 turn of +2.7 = negligible.\n\nLet me be a bit safer: buy 2 supply now (12) → 75; hold. Next turn sell 6 ore → 91 → build mine (80) → 11. Hmm.\n\nActually, let me think about what's smarter: 补给厂 (200) is the structural fix. Every turn I spend on a mine delays it by ~5 turns... but a mine is permanent income too.\n\nLet me quantify: if I build the mine (80 now), income becomes 7 ore/turn = ~19/turn gross; upkeep 11 → net 8/turn → 补给厂 in (200-7)/8 ≈ 24 turns.\nIf I don't build the mine: net 6/turn → 补给厂 in ~19 turns.\nHmm interesting — the mine delays 补给厂 by 5 turns but then adds 2.7/turn forever. Over 40 turns, mine total value ≈ 108 (minus the delay cost). Roughly a wash.\n\nBut there's a subtler issue: selling 7 ore/turn pushes the price down more, hurting all mine revenue. My ore sales have kept the price at 2.7-2.9 (baseline 4).\n\nAlternative plan: pause mine building, sell LESS ore (hold), and instead fund 补给厂 by... no, I need income.\n\nHmm, let me think about it differently: what if I build the 补给厂 FIRST and then the mines? After 补给厂, my food+ore get consumed internally (1 food + 1 ore per turn per 2 armies), so extra mines feed the factory rather than the market. That's the synergy. So 补给厂 first is right.\n\nDecision: skip the mine this turn. Save for 补给厂. Buy 2 supply now (12) → 75.\n\nActually wait — can I get gold faster? What about selling the remaining wood (11, price 1.6)? Need 12 wood for 补给厂! So I should keep wood ≥12. Currently 11 + 2/turn. Fine.\n\nAnd food: 7 held; 补给厂 needs 1 food/turn; food income 4/turn. Fine.\n\nSo: buy 2 supply (12) → 75. Then next turn sell 6 ore (+16) → 91 - supply...\n\nHmm, alternatively: hold the ore (don't sell at 2.7) and sell food? No.\n\nLet me reconsider: I could reach 200 faster by liquidating the 3 new tiles' expected income... no.\n\nOK: buy 2 supply, end turn.\n\nActually, one more idea to raise cash: the newly captured plains tiles (浩轩 3 farmland, 瑞台 1 farmland 2 wood, (11,29) unknown) — farms are bad investments at food 1.0. Skip.\n\nLet me also double check: should I sell equipment? 0. No.\n\nExecute: buy 补给 2.",
            "tool_calls": [
              {
                "id": "call_a62189f30dbe46dc9827ba50",
                "type": "function",
