 To speed it up, sell more aggressively (food/wood too) since holding at trough has weak upside if the trough is caused by others' dumping.\n\nActually, let me quantify the \"hold\" option: if food recovers to 2.0 in ~5-8 turns, selling 19 food later nets 38 vs 21 now → +17. Meanwhile the delay costs ~2-3 turns of factory income (8/turn = ~20). Roughly a wash. So it doesn't matter much either way. Let me sell food/wood surpluses moderately to keep the factory timeline moving, and hold ore (my main product — sell ~4/turn instead of 7 to let the price drift up? Hmm).\n\nLet me just do a simple, robust policy: sell all ore each turn (main income), sell food down to ~10, keep wood ≥12 for the factory (currently 5 — need to accumulate; income 2/turn minus 1 fuel = +1/turn → 12 by turn 29).\n\nHmm, the wood requirement (12) is annoying. Alternatively sell wood now at 1.6 and buy back at 2.0 later? Loss. Let me just keep wood and let it grow.\n\nWait, actually — I could build a lumber camp at 曜野 (森林, 木头x3, 0 buildings): cost 50×1.15 = 57.5 + 5 wood → produces 1 wood/turn (1.6 value) → payback 36 turns. Not worth it for gold, but it accelerates the 12-wood requirement for the factory... which I can also just wait for. Skip.\n\nSo this turn (22):\n1. Sell ore 6 → +16 → 31.\n2. Sell food 8 → +8 → 39. (Keep 11 food.)\n3. Buy supply 4 → -24 → 15. Warehouse 3+4-2 = 5.\n4. Attack (12,29)P with both armies (60/64 HP) → likely capture, armies → ~35/39.\n\nHmm, is attacking now wise given I want to save cash? The attack doesn't cost extra (supply consumption is the same whether resting or attacking). And it gains a tile. Yes, attack.\n\nWait, but one thing to check: (12,29)P is adjacent to 琉州 (11,29) ✓ (dx=1).\n\nAlso, should I instead send them for (11,24)P / (10,23)P (plains near home, adjacent to 兴礁/光崖)? Those are 5-6 tiles away from 琉州 — a long march through hostile terrain (each step through a barbarian tile requires attacking it). Not efficient. Continue the eastern plains chain: (12,29)P → then (13,...) new tiles revealed.\n\nHmm, one concern: expanding east/southeast takes me farther from home; the armies would be deep in newly conquered land. That's fine (they carry their own supply from the warehouse — supply is national, not local? \"补给厂...产补给2\" and \"仓空军队挨饿\" — the warehouse is national, so armies anywhere draw from it).\n\nOK, let me also think: should I use this turn's cash to buy equipment at 8.1 (near baseline) for a future recruit? No — recruiting more armies increases supply drain before the factory exists. Bad.\n\nLet me execute:\n1. sell 矿石 6\n2. sell 粮食 8\n3. buy 补给 4\n4. attack (12,29) with [1,2]\n\nThen end turn.",
